text:
The invention provides a system and a method for instantly removing portrait objects in a film The system comprises an image capturing module,  a signal receiving module,  an object detecting module and a repairing image generating module According to the invention,  the object detection model,  the image repair model and the object tracking algorithm are executed on different hard bodies according to the calculation amount,  so that the energy consumption load of the photographic device is effectively reduced,  the time delay is reduced,  and the repair stability is enhanced When the user takes a picture,  he can obtain a picture containing the current background and the person he wants to appear. WYSIWYG without post-processing In addition,  the present invention optimizes the existing image repair model architecture to reduce the delay bottleneck during upsampling operations. A method for real-time removal of human figures from a video,  applied to provide a real-time preview of the retouched image before taking a photograph,  is executed through a photographic device having an image capturing unit,  a central processing unit,  memory,  a touch screen,  and a neural network processor. It balances the real-time preview and the stability of the retouching process before taking the photograph,  and includes the following steps : 
 The image capturing unit continuously captures video of a target area,  and the video is composed of multiple images captured from the target area,  which are then presented sequentially on the touch screen.
 An object detection model operating on the neural network processor sequentially identifies multiple humanoid objects in each frame of the image,  dynamically generates a humanoid object mask based on the boundary of each humanoid object,  and tracks the identification code corresponding to each humanoid object across frames using an object tracking algorithm operating on the central processing unit,  and temporarily stores it in the memory.
 The touchscreen receives multiple click locations from the user on multiple frames of video starting from a start image; 
 The object detection model is used to find multiple target humanoid objects corresponding to the click locations and a target identification code corresponding to each target humanoid object,  wherein each click location falls within the boundary of a target humanoid object; 
 The central processing unit reads the target identification codes and sequentially receives the humanoid object mask corresponding to the target humanoid object to each image after the starting image; 
 After the camera receives a confirmation signal from the user,  an image inpainting model operating on the neural network processor generates inpainted images on subsequently received images based on the humanoid object masks received by the central processing unit. These inpainted images remove humanoid objects other than the target humanoid objects and generate background-related images at the deletion points;  and
 The touch screen is used to sequentially replace the video with these repaired images.

The invention relates to a fast transport device combination suitable for humanoid robots,  which is composed of a bicycle unit,  a first magnetic base,  a second magnetic base and a movable magnetic element. The bicycle unit can provide fast transport function on a plurality of terrain roads. The movable magnetic element can receive the first magnetic base and the second magnetic base The magnetic force output by the second magnetic base can make the humanoid robot obtain the function of safe connection. The first magnetic base and the second magnetic base can receive the vertical downward dynamic output force of the humanoid robot when it stands horizontally in balance,  so that the bicycle can The rear wheel body part of the unit remains horizontally balanced and the bicycle unit can be lowered The probability of rapid transportation damage caused by the unbalanced dumping of the meta-level can achieve the goal of improving the operational safety probability of rapid transportation of the humanoid robot on a plurality of terrain roads. A rapid transport device assembly suitable for humanoid robots comprises a bicycle unit,  a first magnetic base,  a second magnetic base,  and a movable magnetic element. The bicycle unit can rapidly transport the movable magnetic element across various types of terrain,  as can the first magnetic base and the second magnetic base. The movable magnetic element can receive the magnetic force output from the first magnetic base,  enabling a secure connection between the humanoid robot and the first magnetic base. The magnetic element can receive the magnetic force output from the second magnetic base,  enabling a safe connection between the humanoid robot and the second magnetic base. The first magnetic base can receive the vertically downward dynamic force output by the humanoid robot,  and the second magnetic base can also receive the vertically downward dynamic force output by the humanoid robot,  keeping the rear wheel of the bicycle unit horizontally balanced. This reduces the probability of damage during rapid transportation caused by the bicycle unit tipping over due to horizontal imbalance,  thereby improving the operational safety of the humanoid robot during rapid transportation on various types of terrain and roads. Its features include :  
The number of movable magnetic elements is multiple;  
The upward-facing side of the movable magnetic element is connected to the bottom of the lower limb of the humanoid robot;  
The downward-facing bottom surface of the movable magnetic element is connected to the first magnetic base. 
The downward-facing bottom surface of the movable magnetic element is connected to the second magnetic base. 
The bicycle unit is located between the first magnetic base and the second magnetic base;  
The first magnetic base is connected to the side of the rear wheel section of the bicycle unit;  
The second magnetic base is connected to the other side of the bicycle unit's rear wheel body.

The invention provides an object touch identification method,  which comprises the following steps of :  detecting a human body of an image to generate a human body whole body in the image;  and identifying the image with the human body whole body by using an action identification model to generate human body attributes The humanoid position and humanoid action are then used to generate article categories based on the humanoid position and article configuration information. Finally,  based on the humanoid attributes and humanoid actions generated by the action recognition model and the article categories generated by the article configuration information,  article touch information containing human actions on the article is generated. This achieves more accurate retail sales Touch identification of merchandise in the field The invention further provides an article touch identification system and a computer program product thereof; ........ A method for identifying objects by touch includes : 
Human detection is performed on the image to generate a full-body human figure in the image; 
A motion recognition model is used to identify the image containing the full body of the human figure,  so as to generate the human figure attributes,  human figure position and human figure motion in the image; 
Based on the humanoid's location and item configuration information,  an item category is generated;  and
Based on the humanoid attributes and humanoid actions generated by the motion recognition model,  and the item category generated based on the item configuration information,  item touch information containing the human's action on the item is generated.

The invention relates to an auxiliary device combination of a humanoid robot and an automatic musical instrument for outdoor performance. The auxiliary device combination is composed of a coated long-sleeved jacket,  a temperature and humidity regulating air supply pipe and a connecting unit. The humanoid robot can move the coated long-sleeved jacket arbitrarily during the performance of the automatic musical instrument through the connecting unit to isolate and reduce the number of automatic musical instruments The interference between the operating noise of the humanoid robot and the temperature and humidity control air supply duct can improve the performance and listening effect of the automatic musical instrument performance. The covered long-sleeved top can guide the control airflow output by the temperature and humidity control air supply duct. Increase the safety probability of outdoor performances of the humanoid robot and increase the connection unit and The connection reliability of the automatic musical instrument can increase the performance operation safety probability of the automatic musical instrument for outdoor performance,  and can achieve the goal of improving the performance and listening effects of the humanoid robot and the automatic musical instrument for outdoor performance under the condition of having a higher performance operation safety probability for outdoor performance A combination of an auxiliary device for a humanoid robot and an automatic musical instrument suitable for outdoor performances,  comprising a wrap-around long-sleeved top,  a temperature and humidity control air supply pipe,  and a connection unit. The humanoid robot can move the connection unit arbitrarily,  and the connection unit can move the automatic musical instrument arbitrarily during performances. The wrap-around long-sleeved top can isolate and reduce the operating noise of the humanoid robot,  and the wrap-around long-sleeved top can isolate and reduce the operating noise of the temperature and humidity control air supply pipe,  thereby improving the listening effect of the automatic musical instrument during performances by reducing the interference of the operating noise. The temperature and humidity control air supply pipe can output regulated airflow to the interior of the wrap-around long-sleeved top. The sleeve-covered top can guide the regulated airflow through the humanoid robot,  thereby increasing the safety of the humanoid robot's outdoor performances by regulating the temperature and humidity of the humanoid robot. The long-sleeved,  enveloping top can guide the regulated airflow through the automatic musical instrument. The long-sleeved,  enveloping top can guide the regulated airflow through the connecting unit,  thereby increasing the reliability of the connection between the connecting unit and the automatic musical instrument,  thereby increasing the safety of the automatic musical instrument's outdoor performances. With a higher safety of outdoor performances,  the performance and listening experience of the humanoid robot and the automatic musical instrument during outdoor performances can be improved. The following features are featured :  
The connection unit is connected to the automatic musical instrument;  
The connection unit is connected to the upper limb of the humanoid robot;  
The wrap-around long-sleeved top is wrapped around the body surface of the humanoid robot;  
The wrap-around long-sleeved top is wrapped around the upper limbs of the humanoid robot;  
The covered long-sleeved top has open holes;  
The opening hole of the wrap-around long-sleeved top can connect the inner space of the wrap-around long-sleeved top with the outer space;  
The opening of the opening hole of the wrap-around long-sleeved top is oriented toward the automatic musical instrument;  
The opening direction of the opening hole of the wrap-around long-sleeved top is toward the connecting unit;  
The temperature and humidity control air supply pipe is located in the space between the wrap-around long-sleeved top and the humanoid robot.

The invention discloses a small coordinated control system which can be arranged in a robot or an automatic on-line manufacturing system. The small coordinated control system comprises a built-in () advanced distributed control hardware body provided with artificial intelligent processors,  wherein the artificial intelligent processors are integrated in a system-on-module () board,  each of the artificial intelligent processors comprises four processors or nodes;  interface with wireless communications such as cameras,  motors,  universal/audio interfaces,  the Internet,  and Bluetooth through 2 extenders to send and receive commands and any other data;  electrically connected to a plurality of sensors for sensing the environment and collecting data from infrared,  tactile,  proximity,  and other types of sensors;  an external host flash computer is dedicated to uploading/downloading firmware,  copying and configuring settings;  a non-volatile memory for storing control algorithms,  profiles and other necessary data;  type I user interface for robot operation,  training and setting;  or Ethernet-type internal star network bypasses the standard bus interface to achieve high-speed communication;  an ethernet switching board enables multiple boards to access the ethernet for internal communications within the star network and external Internet access; . :  "()".; ../2...; ..; /.; .; .; - A small coordinated control system that can be installed in a robot or automated line manufacturing system,  including 
Built-in advanced distributed control hardware with artificial intelligence processors integrated into system-on-module (SOM) boards,  with each SOM comprising four processors or nodes;  
Interfacing with cameras,  motors,  general-purpose I/O,  audio interfaces,  the Internet,  Wi-Fi,  and wireless communications such as Bluetooth via I2C expanders to send and receive commands and any other data;  
electrically connected to a plurality of sensors for sensing the environment and collecting data from infrared,  tactile,  proximity,  and other types of sensors;  
An external host flash computer dedicated to uploading/downloading firmware,  copying and configuring settings;  
a non-volatile memory for storing control algorithms,  configuration files,  and other necessary data;  
An HDMI user interface for robot operation,  training,  and configuration;  
USB C or Ethernet type internal star network bypasses the standard PCI bus interface BUS to achieve high-speed communication;  
An Ethernet switch board enables multiple boards to access the Ethernet network for internal communication within the star network and external Internet access.

The pinhole detection device combines wireless signal detection and image identification technology to identify pinhole candid shooting equipment that continuously sends wireless signals in a specific space and performs identity binding and tracking through humanoid identification. When the connection time exceeds the preset threshold,  the system automatically generates an exception or reminder message and promptly notifies relevant personnel. The invention can effectively improve the security of private spaces such as a dressing room,  a toilet,  a restaurant and the like,  realize remote monitoring and reduce the risk of candid shooting A pinhole detection device,  comprising : 
A pinhole detection unit,  comprising : 
a wireless signal detection module,  receiving a plurality of wireless signals in a monitoring space and obtaining MAC information from each of the wireless signals;  and
a processing module connected to the wireless signal detection module,  and activating a monitoring process in response to the wireless signal detection module receiving the wireless signals having the same MAC information,  wherein a monitoring message is generated according to the MAC information and connection time information is calculated; 
an image recognition unit connected to the pinhole detection unit,  comprising : 
a camera,  activated only after the wireless signal detection module detects the wireless signals,  to capture a space and generate an image;  and
an image processing module connected to the camera,  receiving and analyzing a human figure feature in the image,  and generating human figure recognition information based on different shooting time points,  wherein the human figure recognition information includes the recognized human figure feature and a corresponding shooting time stamp;  and
A security host,  including : 
a transmission module connected to the pinhole detection unit and the image recognition unit,  receiving the monitoring information and the connection time information from the pinhole detection unit,  and the human figure recognition information from the image recognition unit; 
a storage module connected to the transmission module,  storing the monitoring information,  the connection time information,  and the human figure recognition information; 
a signal analysis module connected to the storage module,  generating an abnormality message when the connection time information is greater than a preset time threshold,  the abnormality message including the MAC information and the connection time information; 
an identity binding module connected to the storage module,  analyzing and binding the human identification information corresponding to the MAC information according to the connection time information to generate an identity binding message;  and
A notification module is connected to the signal analysis module and the identity binding module,  generates a warning message according to the abnormal message and the identity binding message,  and transmits the warning message to a server via the transmission module,  so that an electronic device can connect to the server and display the warning message in an application.

The pinhole detection device combines wireless signal detection and image identification technology to identify pinhole candid shooting equipment that continuously sends wireless signals in a specific space and performs identity binding and tracking through humanoid identification. When the connection time exceeds the preset threshold,  the system automatically generates an exception or reminder message and promptly notifies relevant personnel. The invention can effectively improve the security of private spaces such as a dressing room,  a toilet,  a restaurant and the like,  realize remote monitoring and reduce the risk of candid shooting A pinhole detection device,  comprising : 
A setting unit receives a setting instruction and generates a detection period signal according to the setting instruction,  wherein the detection period signal includes a start time information and a shut down time information; 
A pinhole detection unit,  connected to the setting unit,  comprising : 
a wireless signal detection module that is activated according to the activation time information,  receives a plurality of wireless signals in a monitoring space and obtains MAC information in each of the wireless signals,  and stops operating according to the deactivation time information;  and
a processing module connected to the wireless signal detection module,  and activating a monitoring process in response to the wireless signal detection module receiving the wireless signals having the same MAC information,  wherein a monitoring message is generated according to the MAC information and connection time information is calculated; 
an image recognition unit connected to the pinhole detection unit,  comprising : 
a camera that is activated to capture a space and generate an image according to the activation time information and stops operating according to the deactivation time information;  and
an image processing module connected to the camera,  receiving and analyzing a human figure feature in the image,  and generating human figure recognition information based on different shooting time points,  wherein the human figure recognition information includes the recognized human figure feature and a corresponding shooting time stamp;  and
A security host,  including : 
a transmission module connected to the pinhole detection unit and the image recognition unit,  receiving the monitoring information and the connection time information from the pinhole detection unit,  and the human figure recognition information from the image recognition unit; 
a storage module connected to the transmission module,  storing the monitoring information,  the connection time information,  and the human figure recognition information; 
a signal analysis module connected to the storage module,  generating an abnormality message when the connection time information is greater than a preset time threshold,  the abnormality message including the MAC information and the connection time information; 
an identity binding module connected to the storage module,  analyzing and binding the human identification information corresponding to the MAC information according to the connection time information to generate an identity binding message;  and
A notification module is connected to the signal analysis module and the identity binding module,  generates a warning message according to the abnormal message and the identity binding message,  and transmits the warning message to a server via the transmission module,  so that an electronic device can connect to the server and display the warning message in an application.

A console includes :  a chair;  the handle assembly includes a slide rail,  a fixed slide block,  a guide fixing plate,  and a control handle group;  the handle assembly has a plurality of sensors;  two safety belts are arranged on the chair A shoulder operating rod group connected to the safety belt and including a fixed frame,  a movable rod,  a rotating part,  two fixed belt parts and a support rod;  a waist operating rod group connected to the safety belt and including a control seat,  a lower fixed frame,  a lower rotating member,  a lower movable rod and two lower fixed belt members;  the handle assembly with the microcomputer control panel and the safety belt are used to drive the shoulder operating rod group and the waist operating rod group,  and the script number is selected through the sensor or the number of the key of the operating handle group to transmit the pre-written action script. manual or automatic control signal A control console,  comprising : 
A chair comprising a seat,  four legs,  and a backrest;  wherein the legs are provided at the four corners below the seat,  a crossbar is provided between the legs at the rear end of the seat,  the backrest extends upward from the rear end of the seat,  and the upper portion of the backrest is provided with two corresponding through-holes; 
A handle assembly is provided on both sides of the chair,  and the handle assembly has a microcomputer control panel and includes a slide rail,  a fixed slider,  a guide fixing plate,  and a control handle group;  wherein,  the slide rail is provided on both sides of the seat portion of the chair,  the inner side of the fixed slider is vertically provided on the slide rail and has an embedded slide rail at its upper and lower ends respectively,  the front end of the fixed slider is provided with the guide fixing plate,  the front end of the guide fixing plate has a vertical horizontal guide,  and the control handle group is provided on the vertical horizontal guide;  the vertical horizontal guide of the fixed slider includes a staggered movable semicircular guide frame and a movable guide frame,  the center of the movable semicircular guide frame is provided with a guide groove,  and both sides of the movable guide frame are provided with a side frame fixed to both sides of the fixed slider as a rotating axis;  the control handle group includes a pull rod,  a telescopic arm,  a joint rotating portion,  a A movable front handle group,  an operation panel group and a UI button group;  wherein the inner end of the pull rod is arranged on the movable guide frame of the vertical and horizontal guide and is inserted into the guide groove of the movable semicircular guide frame;  the telescopic arm is connected to the outer end of the pull rod,  the outer end of the telescopic arm has the joint rotation part,  the outer end of the joint rotation part is connected to the movable front handle group and has the UI button group at the front end,  and the upper end of the movable front handle group is provided with the operation panel group;  the side frame of the vertical and horizontal guide is provided with a sensor,  a sensor is provided between the upper end of the movable semicircular guide frame and the guide fixing plate,  a sensor is provided between the pull rod of the control handle group and the telescopic arm,  a sensor is provided between the telescopic arm and the joint rotation part,  a sensor is provided at the lower end of the movable front handle group,  and a sensor is provided between the movable front handle group and the joint rotation part; 
A second safety belt is provided on the chair,  the safety belt being passed through the through hole of the chair and having a retractable bag at the other end,  the retractable bag being fixed to the crossbar of the chair,  one end of the safety belt being buckled with a front buckle provided at the center of the front end of the seat portion of the chair; 
A shoulder operating lever assembly is provided at the rear end of the backrest of the chair and corresponds to the through-hole. The shoulder operating lever assembly has a microcomputer control panel and includes a fixed frame,  a movable rod,  a rotating member,  two fixed belt members,  and a support rod. The fixed frame is a frame and is fixed to the center of the backrest between the through-holes. The rotating member is provided inside the fixed frame and has a sensor. The movable rod is inserted through the fixed frame and centrally fixed to the rotating member. The fixed belt members for fixing the safety belt are respectively provided on both sides of the movable rod corresponding to the through-holes of the backrest. The support rod is fixed outside the fixed frame to support the safety belt extending to the lower section of the backrest of the chair.
A lumbar operating lever assembly is provided at the back end of the chair,  the lumbar operating lever assembly has a microcomputer control panel and includes a control seat,  a lower fixed frame,  a lower rotating member,  a lower movable rod and two lower fixed belt members;  the upper end of the control seat is connected to the lower fixed frame and has a sensor therebetween;  the control seat is fixedly provided at the middle section of the back end of the chair,  the lower rotating member is provided on the inner side of the center of the lower fixed frame and has a sensor;  the lower movable rod is sleeved in the center of the lower fixed frame and fixed to the lower rotating member;  the lower fixed belt members connected to the safety belt are provided on both sides of the lower movable rod,  and the lower fixed belt members connected to the safety belt correspond to the shoulder operating lever assembly provided on the movable rod and straddled on the support rod; 
The handle assembly with the microcomputer control panel and the safety belt drive the shoulder operating lever assembly and the waist operating lever assembly,  and transmit control signals through the sensor.

The utility model provides an external expansion charging device of a human-shaped machine,  which comprises a body movably arranged on the human-shaped machine,  wherein the body is movably arranged on the human-shaped machine And an operation processing unit electrically connected to a data and power transmission interface,  an environment-aware expansion module,  a power expansion system and a second operating mode data library,  the components being disposed in the body By allowing the human-shaped robot originally configured to perform the first operating mode in the first application scene to wear the external expansion device,  the intelligent brain of the human-shaped robot can obtain the second operation through the information and the power transmission interface. The information stored in the mode of operation simultaneously drives the environment-aware expansion module and the power expansion system Increase the applicable scenarios of human robots in the shortest time and at the lowest cost to improve versatility. An external expansion device for a humanoid robot,  applicable to the humanoid robot,  capable of executing a conventional first operation mode,  the external expansion device comprising : 
a main body,  which is movably disposed on the body trunk of the humanoid robot; 
a processing unit,  a data and power transmission interface,  an environment sensing expansion module,  a power expansion system,  and a second operation mode database,  which are disposed in the body,  and the data and power transmission interface,  the environment sensing expansion module,  the power expansion system,  and the second operation mode database are electrically connected to the processing unit;  and
A plurality of environmental sensors are disposed on the main body and electrically connected to the environmental sensing expansion module; 
The main body is configured on the body trunk of the humanoid robot,  and the data and power transmission interface forms a data and power connection with the humanoid robot,  so that the humanoid robot can read the second operation mode information stored in the second operation mode database,  the power of the power expansion system,  and the environmental information received by the environmental perception expansion module,  so that the humanoid robot executes the second operation mode.

An object of the present invention is to provide a humanoid modeling device capable of easily generating an action path of an humanoid that does not interfere with a surrounding object even under various circumstances The robot modeling device is configured to model an action and equipment setting part,  a deciding part,  an inserting part,  and a generating part of the robot in a virtual space The setting department sets the points of interest at the complex number of locations of the robot. The determination department sets the first point of interest of the complex number of points of interest that have been set as the first base position to determine the first movement position where the robot has moved a predetermined distance. The insertion part inserts the first midpoint between the first base position and the first movement position when the determined first movement position is on the path of the robot movement and the robot does not interfere with the peripheral object. The position generation part sets the first midpoint as the second base position. The insertion of the midpoint is repeated to generate the action of the robot that does not interfere with the peripheral object Road radius. A robot simulation device is a robot simulation device that simulates the movement of a robot in a virtual space and has :  
a setting unit for setting focus points at a plurality of positions of the robot;  
a determination unit that sets a first focus point among the plurality of focus points that have been set as a first reference position to determine a first movement position in which the robot is moved by a predetermined distance;  
an inserting unit that inserts a first intermediate point between the first reference position and the first moving position when the determined first moving position is on a moving path of the robot and the robot does not interfere with surrounding objects;  and 
The generating unit sets the first intermediate point as the second reference position and repeatedly inserts the intermediate points,  thereby generating a motion path of the robot that does not interfere with the surrounding objects.

The present invention can provide a terminal device that can simply photograph a subject to measure biological information of the subject The terminal device (100) includes :  a data acquisition unit (11) that acquires an image of a measurement subject photographed by the photographing unit (2);  an inclination detecting unit (13) detects the inclination of the face of the person to be measured in the picture surface of the display unit (4) based on the face image of the person to be measured included in the image captured by the capturing unit;  and a display control unit (17) for displaying a first target image matching with the inclination of the face portion detected by the inclination detecting unit and an image including the person to be measured displayed on the face of the display unit in a duplicate manner. A terminal device including :  
Photography Department;  
display part;  
an information acquisition unit that acquires the image of the person being measured captured by the imaging unit as information for measuring the biological information of the person being measured;  
a tilt detection unit that detects the tilt of the face of the person being measured in the screen of the display unit based on the face image of the person being measured included in the image captured by the shooting unit;  and 
The display control unit superimposes and displays the first index image matching the inclination of the face detected by the inclination detection unit on the image including the person being measured on the screen of the display unit.

The invention discloses a safe moving gait control method for an adsorption type hexapod pipeline robot. The method comprises the following steps of :  firstly,  determining an initial state configuration of the robot before moving; then based on the initial state configuration and switching rules,  generate the foot end trajectory of the robot moving from the initial state to the landing state; and correcting the foot end track; based on the corrected foot end track,  the joint angle configuration sequence of each joint in the process from the initial state to the foot falling state is generated; finally,  according to the determined joint angle configuration sequence,  the robot is controlled to execute actions and move along the pipe wall. The invention can safely and effectively realize the gait control of the robot moving 360 ° on the inner and outer walls of the pipeline,  thereby solving the problems of uncontrollable adsorption state,  low movement safety,  and load capacity of the adsorption multi-legged robot during the climbing movement process against gravity. 1. An adsorption type six-foot pipeline robot safe moving gait control method,  wherein it comprises the following steps :  S1,  determining the initial state configuration of the robot before moving;  the robot comprises a robot main body and six supporting legs connected with the robot main body through the joint,  the six supporting legs have the same structure and are symmetrically distributed along the robot main body;  the supporting leg comprises three sections of brackets arranged in turn;  the adjacent two sections of brackets are connected by a joint;  the initial state configuration of the robot is the joint angle of the position of each joint of the robot;  S2,  generating the switching rule of the robot moving from the initial state to the foot falling state;  S3,  based on the initial state configuration and the switching rule,  generating a foot end track of the robot moving from the initial state to the foot falling state;  S4,  using the following formula,  correcting the foot end point coordinate in the foot end track T1 of the six supporting legs of the robot determined in the step S3,  wherein the corrected foot end track is T2;  In the formula,  representing the foot falling coordinate of the mth supporting leg foot end determined in the step S3;  
 represents the foot falling coordinate of the mth supporting leg foot end after being corrected;  dp represents the track deviation,  dp=kv (sgn (pmin-p) + 1) t,  kv is the speed coefficient of foot end motion,  pmin represents the minimum air pressure value satisfying the adsorption condition,  p represents the actual foot end air pressure value;  t represents the time taken for the foot end to move from the last foot end coordinate to the current position;  
 representing the Z-axis coordinate of any point of the pipeline axis in the robot coordinate system;  S5,  generating a joint angle configuration sequence in the process of each joint from the initial state to the foot falling state based on the corrected foot end track;  S6,  according to the determined joint angle configuration sequence,  controlling the robot to execute action and move along the wall surface of the pipeline.

The present invention relates to a system and method for identifying safety behavior and voice with private protection. The system includes at least one monitoring host machine and a monitoring rear unit. The monitoring host machine uses a red external line lens to The thermal image of the photographed person at the place to be monitored is photographed,  and the monitoring host machine records the sound or environment of the person at the place through a radio receiver Sound sound and analysis of each frame thermal image to determine the humanoid movements in the thermal image and recognition of the recorded sound to identify human sound or environmental sound When the person's actions or the person's sound or environmental sound meet the conditions for issuing a warning message,  the monitoring host shall issue a warning message to the monitoring platform so that the management person of the monitoring platform may immediately discover violent dialogue by the illuminated person Possible dangerous sounds or actions such as emergency call for help,  sleeping,  falling or long-term inactivity are required and can be disposed of immediately. A privacy-protecting dangerous behavior and semantic identification system,  including :  
At least one monitoring host is installed in an environmental location to monitor the status of personnel in the environmental location. Each monitoring host includes :  
A control unit is connected to at least one infrared lens and at least one radio microphone;  wherein,  the infrared lens continuously captures the environmental location to obtain a plurality of frames of thermal images,  and the radio microphone continuously records the voices of people or environmental sounds in the environmental location;  
A computing unit is connected to the control unit and receives the plurality of frames of thermal images,  the person's voice,  or the environmental sound through the control unit. The computing unit uses a trained AI humanoid detection model to continuously receive the Multiple frames of thermal images are analyzed to determine whether there is a human figure in an effective detection area in the plurality of frames of thermal images and the movements of the humanoid within a monitoring range,  and a trained AI semantic analysis model is used to analyze the human figure. Recognize the human voice or the environmental sound to identify the human voice or the environmental sound;  wherein,  when the action behavior of the humanoid meets the conditions for issuing a warning message,  the AI humanoid detection model sends the warning message;  Among them,  when the person's voice or the environmental sound meets the conditions for issuing the warning message,  the AI semantic analysis model sends the warning message;  wherein the warning message includes sitting for a long time,  falling,  danger,  or being stationary for a long time. At least one of the action,  the person's voice,  or the environmental sound of moaning for help,  violent conversations,  emergency self-help calls for help;  
A memory unit connected to the control unit and the computing unit for storing data and programs;  
An input/output unit is connected to the control unit and the computing unit. The input/output unit includes at least one transmission interface for establishing connections and data transmission between the monitoring host and other external devices;  
A monitoring backend communicates with each monitoring host. The monitoring backend includes :  
A cloud host communicates with each monitoring host to receive the multiple frames of thermal images captured by each monitoring host,  receives the person's voice or the environmental sound recorded by each monitoring host,  and receives the warning message sent by each monitoring host;  
Click on a certain host to connect to the cloud host and display the warning message;  
Among them,  the AI humanoid detection model performs the following process when identifying each frame of thermal image :  
Determine whether the human figure in the thermal image is within the effective detection area,  if not,  discard the human figure;  
Each humanoid in the effective detection area is assigned an identification code (ID). When the humanoid leaves the effective detection area,  its ID is removed;  
Identify the action of the humanoid and add one to the counter value corresponding to the action;  
Among them,  when the AI humanoid detection model determines that the humanoid in the thermal image is located in the effective detection area,  the AI semantic analysis model performs the following process :  
Identify the person's voice or the environmental sound,  and give one point to the person's voice or the environmental sound for keywords with different weight levels in the corpus,  or words related to danger and safety semantics;  
Wherein,  when the count value of the action of the humanoid has accumulated to a threshold value,  or when the integral of the human voice or the environmental sound exceeds a set threshold value,  the computing unit sends a warning message.

This book relates to a teaching aid for the prevention and treatment of sarcopenia. It mainly includes a number of cards. The number of cards divides food,  food,  and food according to their inner content Models such as exercise and risk avoidance factors allow players to easily learn awareness and concepts to prevent sarcopenia during play and integrate awareness and concepts during play into life and use positive diet management and exercise training to achieve effective sarcopenia prevention and treatment in daily life A board game teaching aid for the prevention and treatment of sarcopenia,  which includes :  
A card unit contains a number of cards. The cards are rectangular and have opposite front and back sides. The cards are divided into a diet module card and a sports module according to the content on the reverse side. A set of cards and a card of a risk factor avoidance module;  
A game drawing unit includes a muscle-building cognitive game drawing,  a bingo game drawing,  a muscle-building dinner plate drawing and a muscle-building exercise drawing,  and the card unit is selected according to the game type to match the muscle-building cognitive game drawing. The cards of the diet module,  the cards of the exercise module and the cards of the risk factor avoidance module related to the game drawing,  the bingo game drawing,  the muscle-building dinner plate drawing and the muscle-building exercise drawing are respectively Place it on the muscle-building cognitive game drawing,  the bingo game drawing,  the muscle-building dinner plate drawing and the muscle-building exercise drawing.

An intelligent arithmetic engine system is provided with the core engine and includes the training learning module and the inference judgment module. The core engine 1 is connected with a model optimization module and an algorithm module The problem of traditional inability to eliminate the inability to identify multiple characters in image information is achieved through the establishment of humanoid profiles through the discernment of individual human bodies;  the image data does not include but is not limited to the size of the object The distribution position (the person can be located at any position in the information),  the opposite position is not fixed,  and various positions and clothing covers (such as the person is covered by trees,  objects,  others,  self-wearing clothes,  etc.) can be directly recognized by the person's rhythm point to establish the person's outline and further recognize the posture of the object An intelligent calculation engine system is characterized by :  the intelligent calculation engine system includes :  
An AI core engine is used to train and learn image data and complete humanoid outline and posture recognition. The AI core engine includes but is not limited to an AI training and learning module and an AI reasoning and judgment module that are interconnected;  The AI training and learning module is a module that trains and learns the image data. It completes model establishment through including but not limited to supervised learning and unsupervised learning;  the AI reasoning and judgment module uses the AI The model generated by the training learning module recognizes the humanoid outline and posture in the input image data. It captures each joint and feature node of the character and compares it with the node positions established in the model to establish the humanoid outline. And compare the mutual positions of these nodes to define the most suitable posture completion;  
A model optimization module is connected to the AI core engine. The model optimization module provides an output model and an optimization model respectively;  and improves the performance and accuracy of the AI core engine calculation and recognition,  including but not limited to machine Learning development operations (MLOps),  data mediation,  and data cleaning complete operations including but not limited to minimizing or directly clearing the deviation value of the data source to ensure that the calculation and recognition of the AI core engine are in a state of continuous optimization in every operation. ;  
An algorithm module is connected to the AI core engine. The algorithm module also provides selection algorithms and provided algorithms;  and provides algorithms and optimization methods for all including but not limited to identification,  observation,  analysis,  etc. This algorithm includes but is not limited to sports action analysis algorithms,  etc.,  and can be used to calculate characteristics optimized with the best performance for various human parameters including but not limited to speed,  explosive power,  agility,  balance,  coordination,  etc. The AI core engine and the model optimization module are combined with algorithms dedicated to recognition speed to provide training and recognition operations;  
The acquired character or/object image material is input and submitted to the AI training learning module of the AI core engine to train a model result,  and then the AI inference and judgment module performs humanoid outline recognition,  that is,  the humanoid outline is established,  and It can perform posture recognition;  the model optimization can be completed through actual performance evaluation and integration with the actual calculation every time the image data is input to the calculation or self-training process. The algorithm module provides a characteristic algorithm to have Calculation effect of optimization effect.

The present disclosure relates to a storage system and a human-robot adjustment method. The storage system includes a travel region,  at least two human-robot and a controller The progression region is divided into cells. at least two robots are configured to be piloted along the progression region and each robot occupies one cell The controller is configured to control the loading mechanism of two robots located in two cell grids when the preset conditions are satisfied. The loading mechanism is configured to place the cargo. This system controls the vertical arrangement of the loading mechanisms of two robots located in two adjacent cells when the preset conditions are met to compensate for the loading mechanisms of the two robots located in the same height position. The positional interference caused when performing corresponding actions can reasonably reduce the area of the cell occupied by each robot More robots can be arranged in the same area of travel areas to improve space utilization in the travel areas. ;  ...;  ..... A warehousing system,  the warehousing system includes :  
The marching area is divided into several cells (6);  
At least two robots are configured to travel along the travel area,  and each robot occupies one of the cells (6);  
The controller is configured to control the vertical staggered arrangement of the load-carrying mechanisms (2) of the two robots located in the two adjacent cells (6) when the preset conditions are met,  wherein the load-carrying mechanisms (2) 2) Constructed for placement of cargo (4).

An air quality inspection system in which an air pollution detection unit generates an air quality abnormality signal when air quality information is abnormal The image unit includes a thermal sensing module,  a video module,  a rotating module,  a human shape recognition module and a smoke hazard warning module The thermal sensing module operates according to the air-gas quality abnormality signal and generates a rotation signal when the heat source temperature meets the preset temperature conditions. The imaging module captures environmental monitoring and control images based on the air-gas quality abnormality signal The transfer module moves the camera module according to the transfer signal to position the heat source within the heat source monitoring area of the environmental monitoring image The humanoid recognition module determines whether the environmental monitoring image conforms to the preset humanoid condition when it has the environmental monitoring image and conforms to the preset temperature condition Tobacco Warning The smoking warning is generated when the preset temperature and preset humanoid conditions are met ;  ..... An air quality inspection system,  including :  
An air pollution detection unit includes a connected air quality detection module and an air quality storage module. The air quality detection module detects air quality information and generates a signal when abnormality of the air quality information is detected. An air quality abnormality signal,  the air quality storage module stores the air quality information;  
An imaging unit connected to the air pollution detection unit,  including :  
a transmission module that receives the abnormal air quality signal and the air quality information from the air pollution detection unit;  
A heat sensing module is connected to the transmission module and activated based on the abnormal air quality signal to sense heat source information of a heat source. The heat source information includes a heat source position and a heat source temperature,  and when the heat source temperature meets a When presetting the temperature condition,  a rotation signal is generated based on the position of the heat source;  
A camera module,  connected to the transmission module,  captures an environmental monitoring image based on the abnormal air quality signal;  
A rotation module is connected to the camera module and the thermal sensing module,  and drives the camera module to rotate according to the rotation signal so that the heat source is located in one of the heat source monitoring areas of the environmental monitoring image,  so that the camera module is Target the heat source and capture the environmental monitoring image;  
A humanoid recognition module is connected to the camera module,  and when the camera module captures the environmental monitoring image and the thermal sensing module senses that the temperature of the heat source meets the preset temperature condition,  it determines that at least one of the environmental monitoring images is Whether the part meets a predetermined humanoid condition;  and 
A smoke hazard warning module is connected to the thermal sensing module and the humanoid recognition module. The thermal sensing module senses that the heat source temperature meets the preset temperature condition and the humanoid recognition module determines the environmental monitoring image. When at least part of the humanoid meets the preset humanoid condition,  a smoking warning is generated;  and 
A servo unit is connected to the imaging unit,  receives the smoking warning,  the environmental monitoring image and the air quality information transmitted by the imaging unit and generates an evidence search image.

A motion object detection method and circuit are disclosed in which a plurality of frame images are obtained upon sensing a motion object in a scene to divide each frame image into a plurality of blocks and then calculate a brightness and a chromaticity of each block to compare the blocks with a background model to obtain a difference between the blocks One or more inductive areas may be established according to which an event is detected. The motion objects in each inductive area may be detected. The intelligent model of the network algorithm may be used to calculate a trust score of a motion object rate in each image to compare the trust score with a determination according to the motion object rate. ;  ... () A moving object detection method,  running in a circuit system,  includes :  
Obtain consecutive frames of images of a scene;  
Identify a dynamic event in each frame of image,  which divides each frame of image into multiple blocks,  and then calculates the difference between the brightness and chromaticity of each block and a background model frame by frame to identify the dynamic event;  
When the dynamic event in each frame of image is identified,  a region of interest is established based on one or more blocks in which the dynamic event is detected;  and 
detecting a moving object in the region of interest of the one or more frames of images;  
Among them,  if the moving object is detected,  the region of interest is updated according to the position and image characteristics of the moving object,  so that the moving object is detected according to the updated region of interest in subsequent frames of images;  if no The moving object clears the record of the region of interest stored in a memory.

A method for image tracking and display includes the following procedure. A variation detection process,  which determines whether there is a target increase or decrease in an image corresponding to a variable trigger area. A display screen change process,  which adjusts the camera to capture the image corresponding to a trigger bounding frame and outputs the image to a monitor when the result of the variation detecting procedure is “YES”. A stable detection process,  which determines whether a change parameter of the image corresponding to the trigger bounding frame is less than or equal to a predetermined change value. A target detection process,  which performs a target detecting on the image corresponding to the triggered bounding frame and generates an image display frame. An image adjusting process,  which outputs the image corresponding to the range of the image display frame to the monitor. Accordingly,  the method can reduce the variation of the display screen. An image tracking and display method is used in conjunction with a camera lens and a display. The camera lens continuously captures an image. The image is correspondingly set with a trigger bounding box and a variable trigger area,  including : 
A change detection program that determines whether there is an increase or decrease in the number of a target in the image corresponding to the variable trigger area; 
A display screen change procedure,  when the result of the change detection procedure is "yes",  adjust the camera lens to capture the image corresponding to the trigger bounding box range,  and output the image to the display; 
A stable detection procedure to determine whether the variation parameter of the image corresponding to the triggering bounding box is less than or equal to a preset variation value; 
A target detection program performs target detection on the image corresponding to the trigger bounding box and generates an image display frame;  and
An image adjustment program outputs the image corresponding to the image display frame range to the display.

Rotation speed measuring device for vehicle and human shape,  The image radar system for foreign matter invasion includes one main body,  A storage device and a display device are arranged on the machine body,  and a radar detection module is arranged on the machine body. An optical sensing module and a processor. The radar detection module and the optical sensing module are electrically connected to the processor. The optical sensing module and the processor are integrated into a whole,  so that only the body and the display device are needed to detect whether the vehicle is overspeed or driving in violation and judge whether foreign matters or human shapes invade in a monitoring area,  thereby achieving the purposes of real-time monitoring and warning,  and having the advantages of high system integration and short operation time. An image radar system for vehicle speed measurement and intrusion of human figures and foreign objects,  which includes :  
A body,  the body is provided with a radar detection module,  an optical sensing module and a processor,  the radar detection module is electrically connected to the processor,  the radar detection module detects A state of vehicles or objects in a monitoring area to generate a radar detection signal,  the optical sensing module is electrically connected to the processor,  the optical sensing module is used to photograph the vehicles or objects in the monitoring area,  And generate an optical image signal in the form of video or photo image. The processor is equipped with a distance recognition module,  an object moving direction recognition module,  a humanoid detection module,  a license plate recognition module and a network chip. The distance identification module collects and calculates the moving distance based on the radar detection signal to obtain distance identification information,  and the object moving direction identification module collects and calculates the moving direction based on the radar detection signal to obtain To obtain a direction recognition information,  the human shape detection module performs human shape recognition based on the optical image signal to obtain human shape detection information,  and the license plate recognition module performs license plate recognition based on the optical image signal to obtain a license plate recognition information,  the network chip is electrically connected to the distance recognition module,  the object moving direction recognition module,  the humanoid detection module and the license plate recognition module to transmit the distance recognition information,  the direction recognition information,  The humanoid detection information and the license plate identification information;  
A storage device,  the storage device is the network chip connected to the processor for storing the distance identification information,  the direction identification information,  the human figure detection information and the license plate identification information;  
A display device,  the display device is connected to the network chip of the processor,  the display device is equipped with an intelligent fusion computing module,  and the intelligent fusion computing module receives the information sent by the network chip The distance recognition information,  the direction recognition information,  the human figure detection information and the license plate recognition information are calculated,  analyzed and judged to generate a recognition result,  and the display device displays the Real-time image and radar information in the recognition result.

A vehicle speed measurement and humanoid,  foreign object intrusion of the image radar network camera,  comprising a fuselage,  a storage device and a display device,  the fuselage is provided with a radar detection module,  an optical sensing module and a processor,  the radar detection module and the optical sensing module are electrically connected to the processor,  by virtue of the above structure,  the present creation integrates the fuselage of the radar detection module,  the optical sensing module and the processor,  Only the fuselage and the display device can detect whether the vehicle is speeding or driving illegally in the monitoring area,  and determine whether foreign objects or human figures are invading,  so as to achieve the purpose of real-time monitoring and warning,  and also have the advantages of high system integration and short working time. An image radar network camera for vehicle speed measurement and intrusion of human figures and foreign objects,  which includes :  
A body,  the body is provided with a radar detection module,  an optical sensing module and a processor,  the radar detection module is electrically connected to the processor,  the radar detection module detects A state of vehicles or objects in a monitoring area to generate a radar detection signal,  the optical sensing module is electrically connected to the processor,  the optical sensing module is used to photograph the vehicles or objects in the monitoring area,  And generate an optical image signal in the form of video or photo image. The processor is equipped with a distance recognition module,  an object moving direction recognition module,  a humanoid detection module,  a license plate recognition module and an intelligent fusion calculation module. The distance identification module collects and calculates the moving distance based on the radar detection signal to obtain a distance identification information,  and the object moving direction identification module collects and calculates the moving direction based on the radar detection signal ,  to obtain a direction identification information,  the human shape detection module is based on the optical image signal to identify the human shape,  to obtain a human shape detection information,  the license plate recognition module is based on the optical image signal to perform license plate recognition,  to obtain a License plate recognition information,  the intelligent fusion computing module is electrically connected to the distance recognition module,  the object moving direction recognition module,  the humanoid detection module and the license plate recognition module to receive the distance recognition information,  the direction Calculate,  analyze and judge the recognition information,  the human figure detection information and the license plate recognition information,  and generate a recognition result;  
A storage device,  the storage device is connected to the processor through a network,  and is used to store the distance identification information,  the direction identification information,  the human figure detection information,  the license plate identification information,  and the identification results;  
A display device,  which is connected to the processor through a network,  is used to display the real-time image and radar information in the recognition result processed by the intelligent fusion computing module.

