      the host computer includes :  the motion sensing device comprises a motion sensing device and an upper computer processor; 
      an electronic device,  comprising :  the device comprises a processor,  communication equipment,  a motor driving device,  a motor and a limiting board card.

The utility model aims to provide a motor of a foot-type robot,  which can solve the defects of the existing motor of the foot-type robot,  and specifically,  the motor of the foot-type robot comprises a first motor,  a second motor,  a third motor and a fourth motor,  the second motor is perpendicular to the first motor;  the first connecting assembly is arranged between the first motor and the second motor,  and the first connecting assembly is used for connecting the first motor and the second motor;  the third motor and the second motor are coaxially arranged;  the second connecting assembly is arranged between the second motor and the third motor,  and the second connecting assembly is used for connecting the second motor and the third motor;  a cable arranging channel is formed in a motor of the foot-type robot,  and cables of the motor of the foot-type robot are all arranged in the cable arranging channel. By adopting the technical scheme,  the integrated connection of the three joint motors of the foot-type robot can be realized,  and the cable winding of the foot-type robot is avoided through the hollow routing. 1. A motor for a legged robot,  comprising : 
      a first motor; 
      the second motor is perpendicular to the first motor; 
      a first connection assembly disposed between the first motor and the second motor,  the first connection assembly being configured to connect the first motor and the second motor; 
      a third motor disposed coaxially with the second motor;  and
      a second connection assembly disposed between the second motor and the third motor,  the second connection assembly configured to connect the second motor and the third motor; 
      the motor of the foot robot is internally provided with a wire arranging channel,  and cables of the motor of the foot robot are all distributed in the wire arranging channel.

The utility model discloses a motor of a foot type robot. The motor comprises a first motor and a second motor,  the second motor and the first motor are coaxially arranged;  the connecting assembly is arranged between the first motor and the second motor,  and the connecting assembly is used for connecting the first motor and the second motor;  a central shaft of a motor of the foot type robot is provided with a cable arranging hole,  and cables are arranged in the cable arranging hole. By the adoption of the technical scheme,  hollow wiring of the motor of the foot-type robot can be achieved,  winding of cables is prevented,  and normal work of the foot-type robot is guaranteed. 1. A motor for a legged robot,  comprising : 
      a first motor; 
      a second motor disposed coaxially with the first motor;  and
      the connecting assembly is arranged between the first motor and the second motor and is used for connecting the first motor and the second motor; 
      a wire arranging hole is formed in the central shaft of a motor of the foot type robot,  and cables are arranged in the wire arranging hole.

The invention particularly relates to a cross-camera pedestrian track processing method,  a computer device and a readable storage medium. On the basis of yolololov4 detection and pedestrian re-recognition technology ReID as human-shaped matching,  a memory space and a hard disk space of a computer device are combined to carry out pedestrian track splicing. When the pedestrian tracks are spliced,  the corresponding pedestrian tracks are mapped and determined according to different judgment results,  and when the pedestrian tracks are spatially mapped,  the mapped pedestrian trajectories conflict with each other in time or spatially conflict,  so that mutual interference between pedestrians to be spliced can be ensured. In order to ensure the accuracy and the reliability of track splicing,  the multi-dimensional characteristic of the pedestrian can be taken into consideration based on the feature similarity,  so that the global pedestrian track can be completely and accurately determined,  and the phenomena of track disorder,  track loss and the like are avoided. 1. A cross-camera pedestrian track processing method is applied to computer equipment in communication connection with a camera,  pedestrian tracks to be processed are stored in a hard disk space of the computer equipment,  the pedestrian tracks to be processed are imported into the hard disk space from a memory space of the computer equipment,  and the pedestrian tracks in the memory space are generated based on pictures uploaded by the camera,  and the method comprises the following steps : 
      judging whether a preset mapping space is an initialization space; 
      under the condition that the preset mapping space is the initialization space,  mapping a plurality of first to-be-processed pedestrian tracks into the preset mapping space and taking the pedestrian tracks as original pedestrian tracks;  wherein,  the first pedestrian trajectories to be processed conflict with each other in time or space; 
      under the condition that the preset mapping space is a non-initialization space,  mapping a plurality of second pedestrian tracks to be processed into the preset mapping space;  the second to-be-processed pedestrian tracks conflict with each other in time or space,  and the non-initialized space comprises a plurality of original pedestrian tracks which conflict with each other in time or space; 
      determining the feature similarity between each original pedestrian track and each second pedestrian track to be processed aiming at each original pedestrian track in the non-initialized space;  determining a target pedestrian track matched with the original pedestrian track according to the characteristic similarity;  the target pedestrian track is a second pedestrian track to be processed,  which is not conflicted with the original pedestrian track in time and space,  and has a characteristic similarity higher than a set similarity in the second pedestrian tracks to be processed; 
      splicing the original pedestrian track and the target pedestrian track corresponding to the original pedestrian track to obtain a global track corresponding to the original pedestrian track; 
      wherein the pedestrian trajectory in the memory space is generated by : 
      acquiring a picture uploaded by the camera,  and carrying out human shape detection on the picture to obtain a human shape detection frame; 
      judging whether a track to be matched exists in the memory space; 
      if the pedestrian shape detection frame does not exist,  a new pedestrian track is created according to the human shape detection frame and the human shape characteristics corresponding to the detection frame and is stored in the memory space; 
      if yes,  extracting the human-shaped feature corresponding to the current detection frame in the picture,  and calculating a first iou between the current detection frame and the historical detection frame corresponding to the track to be matched;  the historical detection frame is a detection frame of the last moment corresponding to the track to be matched;  and calculating a second iou between every two detection frames except the first iou in the picture; 
      constructing a similarity matrix between the current detection frame and the track to be matched according to the human-shaped feature and the first iou;  selecting k pairs of matching pairs with the similarity larger than a set threshold according to the similarity matrix,  wherein k is not larger than the number of the tracks to be matched and not larger than the number of the detection frames,  and each matching pair corresponds to one track to be matched and one detection frame; 
      when the detection frames which are not successfully matched exist,  according to the second iou,  drawing the detection frames with the iou larger than 0 between the detection frames and the sheltered person into a track which is sheltered by the sheltered person and is lost,  so as to obtain k pairs of matched pairs; 
      and updating the track information corresponding to each track to be matched,  judging whether a target updated track with the lost frame number exceeding a set frame number threshold exists in the updated track after updating,  and if so,  migrating and storing the target updated track to the hard disk space.

The invention relates to a quadruped robot foot end ground contact detection method and system,  and the method comprises the following steps :  S1,  calculating the foot end ground contact height of eachleg,  and calculating the foot end height contact probability of each leg according to the foot end ground contact height of each leg;  calculating the knee joint torque contact probability according to the knee joint torque of each leg;  S2,  according to the gait planning contact probability,  planning the foot end height contact probability and the knee joint torque contact probability of the fourlegs,  utilizing Kalman filtering fusion to obtain the final foot end contact probability of the four legs;  and according to the four-leg foot end contact probability,  judging a foot end ground contactstate. On the premise of not deploying redundant sensors at the foot ends,  the contact state between the foot ends and the ground is accurately estimated by means of the basic sensors of the quadruped robot body and a fusion algorithm,  and the problem of sensor wiring can be solved;  even in a rugged terrain or a step terrain,  a reliable ground contact state can still be obtained. 1. The four-footed robot foot end touchdown detection method is characterized in that :  the method comprises the following steps : 
      s1,  calculating the foot end ground clearance of each leg,  and calculating the foot end height contact probability according to the foot end ground clearance of each leg; 
      calculating the knee joint torque contact probability of each leg according to the knee joint torque of each leg; 
      calculating the contact probability of gait planning according to the gait phase; 
      s2,  obtaining the final four-leg and foot-end contact probability by Kalman filtering fusion according to the gait planning contact probability,  the foot-end high contact probability and the knee joint torque contact probability of the four legs;  and judging the foot end grounding state according to the four-leg foot end contact probability.

The invention provides a device for monitoring ambient air and exhaust gas. The device comprises a first monitoring device case,  monitoring sensors,  herringbone plates,  a conical insulating cover,  a lightning rod,  and a second monitoring device case. The humanoid plates are fixed to vertical supporting rods;  balls are embedded in the upper and lower sides of three outsides of each humanoid plate; and the outer ends of the herringbone plates are arranged in circular ring grooves. Fixing through holes are formed in the outer sides of the T-shaped holes in the upper and lower ends of a fixing plate. Eight sets of outer plates are embedded in the outer circumference of the first monitoring device case and the second monitoring device case,  and the monitoring sensors are embedded in the middleof the two sides of the outer plates. The heights of two sets of monitoring devices are changed by adjusting the heights of transverse supporting frames on the first monitoring device or the second monitoring device,  and air and exhaust gas indexes in the environment with different heights of a monitoring site are detected. The lightning rod is arranged so that the monitoring device is prevented from being struck by lightning. 1. An ambient air and exhaust gas monitoring device,  characterized in that :  the ambient air and exhaust gas monitoring equipment comprises a first monitoring device shell (1),  an outer partition plate (101),  a monitoring sensor (102),  a circular ring groove (103),  a wireless transmitter (104),  a transverse support frame (201),  a threaded hole (2011),  a vertical support rod (202),  a lightning rod through hole (2021),  a herringbone plate (203),  a ball (204),  a fixing plate (3),  a T-shaped hole (301),  a fixing through hole (302),  a conical insulating cover (4),  a lightning rod (5) and a second monitoring device shell (6);  a herringbone template (203) is fixed on the vertical supporting rod (202),  balls (204) are inlaid on the upper side and the lower side of the three groups of outer sides of the herringbone template (203),  a circular groove (103) is formed in the middle of the inner wall of a middle through hole of the first monitoring device shell (1) and the second monitoring device shell (6),  the outer end of the herringbone template (203) is arranged in the circular groove (103),  the transverse supporting frame (201) is welded on one side of the vertical supporting rod (202),  a threaded hole (2011) is formed in the rear end portion of the transverse supporting frame (201),  a T-shaped hole (301) is formed in the middle of the fixing plate (3),  a fixing bolt penetrates through the T-shaped hole (301) and is screwed into the threaded hole (2011) to fix the transverse supporting frame (201) on the fixing plate (3),  and a fixing through hole (302) is further formed in the outer side of the T-shaped hole (301) at the upper end,  eight groups of outer sub-plates (101) are embedded on the peripheries of the first monitoring device shell (1) and the second monitoring device shell (6),  monitoring sensors (102) are embedded in the middles of two sides of each outer sub-plate (101),  the top end of each vertical supporting rod (202) is connected with a conical insulating cover (4),  and a lightning rod through hole (2021) is formed in the middle of each vertical supporting rod (202); 
      the balls (204) on the herringbone plate (203) are respectively contacted with the upper wall and the lower wall in the circular groove (103); 
      the first monitoring device shell (1) and the second monitoring device shell (6) are adjusted in position on the fixing plate (3) through bolts behind the transverse supporting frame (201); 
      the top parts of the first monitoring device shell (1) and the second monitoring device shell (6) are also provided with a wireless transmitter (104); 
      a Pentium microprocessor and a power supply battery are arranged in the first monitoring device shell (1) and the second monitoring device shell (6),  and the Pentium microprocessor,  the monitoring sensor (102) and the wireless transmitter (104) are connected through wires; 
      the lightning rod (5) downwards penetrates through a lightning rod through hole (2021) in the middle of the vertical supporting rod (202) on the first monitoring device shell (1) and penetrates through a lightning rod through hole (2021) in the middle of the vertical supporting rod (202) on the second monitoring device shell (6) to be connected to the bottom end of the fixing plate (3); 
      the front side surface and the rear side surface of the fixed plate (3) are provided with insulating layers; 
      the overall structure of the second monitoring device shell (6) is the same as that of the first monitoring device shell (1); 
      during the use,  according to the difference of monitoring environment and position,  through the height of adjusting horizontal support frame (201) on first monitoring or the second monitoring devices,  change two sets of monitoring devices's height,  thereby to the air in the environment of monitoring place co-altitude,  the waste gas index detects,  during the use under the effect of wind-force or other external forces,  monitoring devices rotates on herringbone template (203),  detect the monitoring index in the air that comes from the equidirectional not,  and pass through wireless transmitter (104) with the numerical value that detects and feed back background monitoring platform,  through setting up lightning rod (5),  in the thunderstorm day,  avoid monitoring devices to be damaged by the thunder and lightning,  improve monitoring devices's life.

The invention provides a seeing-eye robot with a human-machine embodied and tangible interaction function and a working method. The robot comprises a ground device and an embodied and tangible interaction device;  the ground device comprises a cage-shaped spherical shell and an omni-directional rotor-wing unmanned aerial vehicle arranged in the spherical shell;  the omni-directional rotor-wing unmanned aerial vehicle is internally provided with a control device,  and a balance bracket is provided with a laser radar sensor,  a camera,  a GPS module and a motor;  an output shaft of the motor is connected with a fixed wheel,  and a synchronous wheel is connected with a synchronous belt arranged around the circumference of the spherical shell;  the robot is also provided with a top controller,  and thelaser radar sensor,  the camera,  the GPS module,  the motor and the omni-directional rotor-wing unmanned aerial vehicle are all connected to the top controller;  the embodied and tangible interaction device comprises a left interaction device and a right interaction device which have the same structures;  the left interaction device comprises a micro air pump and a micro controller which are arrangedat corresponding positions of the left hand of a blind person and connected with each other,  and the micro air pump is also connected with an airbag;  the embodied and tangible interaction device is connected with the top controller. The seeing-eye robot with the human-machine embodied and tangible interaction function has an all-terrain passing ability and controls and guides the blind person towalk,  so that the blind person has an intuitive feeling. 1. A human body feeling interaction blind-guiding robot is characterized by comprising a ground device and a human body feeling interaction device;  the ground device comprises a cage-shaped spherical shell (9) and an omnidirectional rotor unmanned aerial vehicle (3) arranged in the spherical shell (9);  the omnidirectional rotor unmanned aerial vehicle (3) is internally provided with a control device for controlling the motion attitude thereof;  a balance support (1) is arranged on the spherical shell (9),  and a laser radar sensor (6),  a camera (7),  a GPS module (8) and a motor (4) are arranged on the balance support (1);  an output shaft of the motor (4) is connected with a fixed wheel,  and a synchronous wheel is connected with a synchronous belt (2) arranged along the circumferential direction of the spherical shell (9);  the balance bracket (1) is of an inverted U-shaped structure,  and two ends of the balance bracket are hinged with the spherical shell (9);  the system is also provided with a top controller (5),  and the laser radar sensor (6),  the camera (7),  the GPS module (8) and the motor (4) are all connected with the top controller (5);  the somatosensory interaction device comprises a left interaction device and a right interaction device which are identical in structure;  the left interaction device comprises a micro air pump and a microcontroller which are arranged at the corresponding positions of the left hand of the blind and are mutually connected,  and the micro air pump is also connected with an air bag;  the control device is connected with the top controller (5) and the microcontroller;  the omnidirectional rotor unmanned aerial vehicle (3) comprises four two-degree-of-freedom rotors with the same structure;  the four two-freedom-degree rotor wings are respectively positioned at four vertexes of the regular tetrahedron and are connected with each other through a bracket (28); 
      the two-degree-of-freedom rotor wing comprises an outer ring (15) and an inner ring (16) which are concentrically arranged;  the X-axis servo motor (11) is arranged on the inner ring (16) through a first rudder disc (13);  the Y-axis servo motor (10) is arranged on the outer ring through a second rudder disk (12);  the X-axis servo motor (11) and the Y-axis servo motor (10) are both connected with a direct current brushless motor (23),  and the direct current brushless motor (23) is connected with blades;  the X-axis servo motor (11),  the Y-axis servo motor (10) and the direct current brushless motor (23) are all connected with a control device; 
      and the balance support (1) is also provided with a gyroscope,  and the gyroscope is connected with the top controller (5).

The invention discloses a single-drive bionic multi-legged robot and a reconfiguration steering method thereof. The single-drive bionic multi-legged robot comprises a frame (A),  a left rear leg (B),  aleft front leg (C),  a right rear leg (D) and a right front leg (E). Buffering and energy storage components such as Achilles tendon (E-5),  plantar quadrates (E-9) and a rubber pad (E-11) are mountedon each leg of the robot. The four legs are connected with a motor (A-1) through belt transmission to realize single drive. By linear drive including a push rod,  a hydraulic cylinder and the like mounted in a biceps brachii connecting rod (E-3) in each leg,  leg supporting phase length variation is realized,  and reconfiguration steering is realized. Due to single drive,  the robot is integrally simple in structure,  easy to control and high in reliability. By adding of the elastic components into the legs of the robot,  impact of the legs and the ground is reduced,  and moving efficiency is improved. Reconfiguration steering is provided for a steering control strategy. The single-drive bionic multi-legged robot can be used for military surveillance,  transporting and the like. 1. A reconstruction steering method of a single-drive bionic multi-legged robot is characterized by comprising the following steps : 
      a single-drive bionic multi-legged robot consists of a frame (A),  a left rear leg (B),  a left front leg (C),  a right rear leg (D) and a right front leg (E); 
      the right front leg (E) imitates a leg structure of a cheetah,  and an Archimedes tendon (E-5),  a plantar quadratus (E-9) and a rubber pad (E-11) are arranged in the leg; 
      the right front leg (E) and the left rear leg (B),  the left front leg (C) and the right rear leg (D) have the same mechanical structure,  rod piece shape and assembly mode; 
      the right front leg (E) is a single-drive freedom degree connecting rod mechanism,  and a crank (E-1) is fixedly connected with a right front leg belt wheel (A-13) through a screw;  the mounting hole at the end part of the femur (E-15) is rotationally connected with the front bracket (A-15) through a bolt shaft; 
      the left rear leg (B),  the left front leg (C) and the right rear leg (D) are installed in the same way as the right front leg (E) and are uniformly distributed at four corners of the rack (A); 
      the left rear leg (B),  the left front leg (C),  the right rear leg (D) and the right front leg (E) are connected with a motor through belt transmission to realize single drive; 
      the reconstruction steering method realizes leg size adjustment through linear driving arranged on a biceps brachii connecting rod (E-3) in a right front leg (E),  the linear driving can be realized in a push rod or hydraulic cylinder mode,  the left rear leg (B),  the left front leg (C) and the right rear leg (D) adopt the same adjusting strategy,  and the whole machine forms different foot end tracks on the left side and the right side by changing the size of the leg connecting rod so as to realize steering.

The utility model provides a coal conveying belt anti-crossing device which comprises a controller,  a humanoid target detection algorithm is set in the controller,  and the humanoid can be recognized according to image information. The infrared camera is electrically connected with the controller,  and the infrared camera collects image information of a coal conveying belt site and transmits the image information to the controller;  the loudspeaker is electrically connected with the controller,  the loudspeaker is arranged on the site of the coal conveying belt,  and the controller transmits soundinformation to the loudspeaker;  wherein the sound information is preset information stored in the controller;  and the power supply supplies power to the controller,  the infrared camera and the loudspeaker. The anti-crossing device for the coal conveying belt can automatically detect whether a person moves near the coal conveying belt in the daytime and at night,  and can give an alarm through soundwhen the person is detected,  so that the personal safety of a worker is ensured. 1. A coal conveying belt anti-crossing device is characterized by comprising
      The controller is internally provided with a human-shaped target detection algorithm and can identify human shapes according to image information; 
      the infrared camera is electrically connected with the controller,  collects the image information of the coal conveying belt site and transmits the image information to the controller; 
      the loudspeaker is electrically connected with the controller,  the loudspeaker is arranged on the site of the coal conveying belt,  and the controller transmits sound information to the loudspeaker; 
      the sound information is preset information stored in the controller; 
      and the power supply supplies power to the controller,  the infrared camera and the loudspeaker.

The invention provides a buffering and stability improving humanoid robot foot mechanism. The foot mechanism comprises a foot sole connecting component used for connecting a shank part of a humanoid robot and one or more claw toe mechanisms arranged at the foot of the humanoid robot. Each claw toe mechanism comprises a rack,  a claw tip,  a connecting rod,  a first elastic component and a buffering component,  wherein the claw toe mechanism has a first mode suitable for soft ground walking and a second mode suitable for hard ground walking. The buffering and stability improving humanoid robot footmechanism has a buffering and stability improving function and can adapt to more complex environments,  and the problem that original mechanisms can only walk on the soft ground is solved. 1. A humanoid robot foot mechanism comprising : 
      a sole connection part for connecting a lower leg part of the humanoid robot; 
      one or more claw and toe mechanisms mounted on a foot of the humanoid robot;  each of the claw and toe mechanisms comprises :  the device comprises a rack,  claw tips,  a connecting rod,  a first elastic component and a buffer mechanism;  the claw and toe mechanism has a first mode suitable for walking on soft ground and a second mode suitable for walking on hard ground; 
      the frame is detachably connected with the foot of the humanoid robot;  the first connecting end of the claw tip is connected with the rack through a hinge,  and the second connecting end of the claw tip is connected with one end of the connecting rod through a hinge;  the first elastic component connects the third connecting end of the claw tip with the rack so as to provide restoring force during the foot lifting process of the humanoid robot; 
      the buffer mechanism is characterized by comprising a sliding chute,  a sliding block,  a stop block,  a second elastic component and an elastic retaining mechanism;  the other end of the connecting rod is connected with the sliding block through a hinge;  the sliding block can slide in the sliding groove,  and the second elastic component can apply thrust to the sliding block in the foot lifting process of the humanoid robot;  the elastic retaining mechanism can apply an elastic force to the stop block so as to clamp the sliding block in the sliding groove.

The invention discloses a network connection method for cooperation of a person and a robot. The network connection method comprises the following steps :  1) a terminal equipment production stage;  2) aterminal equipment starting stage;  3) adevice equipment discovery stage;  4) an equipment working stage. According to the invention,  the robot terminal can be assisted in establishing connection withthe client and providing a high-bandwidth low-delay transmission channel as much as possible;  a terminal comprising a plurality of network adapters and an environment for carrying out network access by using a network address and port conversion technology are compatible;  the equipment terminals using the server comprise digital certificates signed and issued by equipment manufacturers in advance; unauthorized equipment terminals or counterfeit terminal equipment are prevented from using the server;  and meanwhile,  the terminal equipment is prevented from being connected to the counterfeit server by verifying the certificate of the server,  and the transmission mode of combining point-to-point connection and the transit server tunnel is adopted,  so that the advantages of low delay,  high bandwidth and high network compatibility of the transit server tunnel of the point-to-point connection can be effectively combined. 1. A network connection method for human-robot collaboration,  comprising the steps of : 
      1) terminal equipment production phase
      1.1) a device manufacturer generating a device certificate authority key pair and a device certificate authority digital certificate; 
      1.2) generating a registration server key pair and a registration server digital certificate issued by an equipment certificate issuing organization,  and deploying the registration server key pair and the registration server digital certificate issued by the equipment certificate issuing organization in a registration server;  presetting a unique identifier,  a terminal equipment key pair and a terminal equipment digital certificate signed by an equipment certificate authority in each terminal equipment; 
      2) terminal equipment starting stage
      2.1) the terminal equipment establishes connection with a registration server through the Internet; 
      2.2) the terminal device tries to discover the router through the universal plug and play protocol and establishes port mapping; 
      2.3) the terminal equipment sends the network interface information to a registration server; 
      2.4) the registration server checks the message after receiving the message,  and returns a response of successful registration after the check is passed; 
      2.5) the terminal equipment sends heartbeat messages to the registration server and reports the network state of the terminal equipment after network change or a period of time; 
      3) device discovery phase
      3.1) controlling the client to start,  if the client is started for the first time,  generating a client authentication key pair,  a client identifier and a client digital certificate; 
      3.2) controlling the client to connect to the registration server,  and sending a device discovery request,  wherein the request contains the unique identifier of the terminal device to be connected; 
      3.3) if the terminal equipment to be found is registered on the registration server and binding is not executed,  sending a binding request to the terminal equipment,  returning a binding agreement reply by the terminal equipment after obtaining user authorization,  simultaneously recording the client identifier in a nonvolatile memory of the terminal equipment,  and if the terminal equipment to be found is registered on the registration server and the bound client identifier is consistent with the record in the nonvolatile memory,  passing authentication; 
      3.4) after the authentication is passed,  the registration server assists in exchanging network addresses,  port numbers,  digital certificates of both parties and tokens for establishing transit connection; 
      3.5) controlling the client and the terminal equipment to try to establish connection by directly using the network address of the other party obtained by exchange,  simultaneously,  both parties use the token provided by the registration server to establish connection in the transfer server,  if the connection is successfully established within the time limit,  the transfer server sends a message to both parties,  and if the connection is not established within the time limit,  the direct connection is abandoned,  and the transfer server forwards all information of both parties; 
      4) working phase of the apparatus
      When the point-to-point connection is interrupted or the connection quality is reduced,  switching to use the relay connection established by the relay server to carry out communication,  and simultaneously trying to reestablish the point-to-point connection;  if the connection with the transit server and the opposite side cannot be reestablished within the limited time and new network interface information of the opposite side is not received from the registration server,  connection reestablishment is abandoned,  the terminal equipment is registered again according to the process of the terminal equipment starting stage,  and the client side redisfinds the terminal equipment according to the process of the equipment discovery stage.

The utility model discloses a toy body capable of being triggered at multiple positions,  which comprises a body,  a plurality of action pieces are arranged on the body,  and each action piece forms a part of the shape of the toy body;  the acousto-optic module is arranged in the body;  the transmission module is movably arranged in the body,  one end of the transmission module is arranged correspondingto the at least two action pieces,  the other end of the transmission module is arranged corresponding to the acousto-optic module,  and the at least two action pieces trigger the same acousto-optic module through the transmission module when acting. The embodiment of the utility model discloses a toy body capable of being triggered at multiple positions. A plurality of action pieces are arranged on the toy body to serve as acousto-optic trigger points,  the action pieces are linked with an integrated electronic function module through a transmission module,  the production and assembly difficulty is effectively reduced,  the reject ratio of products is reduced,  the assembly time is shortened,  the production cost is reduced,  and detection or maintenance of the products is facilitated. 1. A toy body capable of being triggered at multiple places,  which is characterized by comprising : 
      the toy comprises a body,  a handle and a handle,  wherein the body is provided with a plurality of action pieces,  and each action piece forms one part of the shape of the toy body; 
      the acousto-optic module is arranged in the body; 
      the transmission module is movably arranged in the body,  one end of the transmission module corresponds to at least two of the action pieces,  the other end of the transmission module corresponds to the acousto-optic module,  and at least two of the action pieces respectively trigger the acousto-optic module through the transmission module when acting.

The utility model is suitable for the technical field of robots,  and provides a joint structure and a leg-foot robot,  the joint structure comprises a motor assembly,  the motor assembly is provided with a rotating shaft used for outputting power,  and the rotating shaft is a hollow shaft;  the lead screw pair is connected into the rotating shaft and is coaxial with the rotating shaft;  the push rod isconnected with one end of the lead screw pair;  when the rotating shaft drives the lead screw pair to rotate,  the lead screw pair drives the push rod to linearly move along the axis of the rotating shaft;  the legged robot comprises the joint structure. According to the utility model,  compared with a hydraulic system,  the motor is simpler to control and free of oil leakage risk,  and meanwhile,  thelead screw pair has the characteristics of simple structure,  low cost,  low friction coefficient,  high efficiency and the like relative to the speed reducer,  so that the joint structure has the advantages of simple structure,  low cost,  low friction coefficient,  high efficiency,  no oil leakage risk,  simplicity in control and the like. 1. A joint structure,  comprising : 
      the motor assembly is provided with a rotating shaft for outputting power,  and the rotating shaft is a hollow shaft; 
      the screw pair is connected in the rotating shaft and is coaxially arranged with the rotating shaft;  and
      the push rod is connected with one end of the screw rod pair; 
      when the rotating shaft drives the screw pair to rotate,  the screw pair drives the push rod to do linear motion along the axis direction of the rotating shaft.

The invention provides a Chinese chess recognition learning algorithm and a robot intelligent automation system and method based on the algorithm,  and the system comprises a visual robot,  monitoring computers and the like. The system is started,  the visual robot is triggered to collect an image,  chess placing and chess moving operations are realized with the Chinese chess recognition learning algorithm and a Chinese chess decision algorithm by the visual robot who takes part in the Chinese chess playing,  corresponding chess placing and chess moving information is sent to respective monitoringcomputers,  and at the same time,  the monitoring computers display virtual interfaces comprising overall scene information;  autonomous intelligence operation and man-machine coordination operation canbe realized by the robot,  a foundation is laid for working of the intelligent automation system of the robot,  the robot has a high intelligence level and is a typical application of the artificial intelligence technology and the robot technology,  and at the same time,  the provided Chinese chess recognition learning algorithm is rapid in speed and high in accuracy and robustness. 1. A robot intelligent system based on a chess recognition learning method comprises two monitoring computers,  two visual robots participating in chess game,  suckers at the tail ends of the robots,  two matched air pumps,  a metal chess board and a router,  wherein,  the tail end of each visual robot is provided with a camera for collecting the visual images on the metal chess board,  the visual robot executes the chess identification learning method,  and the coordinates of the chess in the image are converted according to a certain proportional relation to obtain the motion coordinates of the robot coordinate system,  corresponding grabbing operation is carried out by utilizing suckers arranged at the respective tail ends and placed at the target position on the chessboard by combining a metal chess chessboard,  the robot installation height and the identified chess type information,  chess moving operation is realized by using a chess decision method,  the chess placing and moving information is broadcasted to another robot participating in the chess game through the local area network; 
      the Chinese chess identification learning method comprises a Chinese chess identification positioning method when Chinese chess is captured,  a chessboard searching method and an identification and classification method for the captured Chinese chess,  wherein the identification and classification method comprises the following steps : 
      collecting a Chinese chess card surface,  namely a front image of the Chinese chess,  wherein the color difference between a Chinese chess front area and a background area forms an RGB color space model constraint condition,  detecting the front edge of the Chinese chess by adopting a contour detection method according to the constraint condition,  selecting the front edge closest to the left lower corner of the Chinese chess board,  and obtaining an external rectangle of the front edge of the Chinese chess to obtain an effective Chinese chess front area;  using a plurality of chess front area images as training samples,  training a Squeeze Net classifier,  inputting pictures cut according to the size of a circumscribed rectangle at the edge of the front of the chess into the trained Squeeze Net classifier,  and obtaining the identification classification category information of the chess through the Squeeze Net classifier,  wherein labels 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8 … 14 respectively correspond to a background and 14 chess pieces; 
      the chess is characterized in that the visual robot collects images above a chessboard of the chess through a terminal camera,  extracts information of colors,  pixel areas,  circle radiuses and circle numbers to obtain external rectangles of the chess pieces,  cuts out pictures at corresponding positions of the external rectangles from an original picture,  sends the pictures into a Squeeze Net classifier to obtain type information of the chess,  and captures and places the type information of the chess at the corresponding positions;  an air pump is arranged between the vision robot and the monitoring computer,  and is matched with a sucker arranged at the tail end of the robot to complete the grabbing operation of the robot in a matching way.

The utility model discloses an intelligent household device capable of improving use convenience,  which comprises a humanoid intelligent robot body,  a holding mechanism is arranged on the robot body, the holding mechanism comprises a connecting ring and a handle assembly,  and the connecting ring is sleeved on the neck part of the robot body;  the handle assembly comprises a limiting ring,  a handle, a tensioning ring and a spring. One side of the limiting ring is connected with the connecting ring;  the handle is located in a center hole of the limiting ring. The handle is U-shaped,  the tail endsof the handle are connected with the side,  close to the robot body,  of the inner wall of the limiting ring,  the tensioning ring and the spring are located on the inner side of the handle,  the end,  close to the robot body,  of the spring is connected with the limiting ring,  the other end of the spring is connected with the tensioning ring,  and when the tensioning ring makes contact with the middleof the handle,  the spring is stretched. The two handle assemblies are symmetrical about the axis center of the connecting ring. Due to the arrangement of the handle assembly,  the convenience for a user to use the robot is improved. 1. Improve intelligent house device of convenience of use,  including humanoid intelligent robot body (1),  its characterized in that :  the robot comprises a robot body (1),  and is characterized in that a holding mechanism is arranged on the robot body (1),  the holding mechanism comprises a connecting ring (2) and a handle assembly,  the connecting ring (2) is sleeved on the neck of the robot body (1),  and the inner diameter of the connecting ring (2) is smaller than the maximum diameter of the head of the robot body (1) and the maximum diameter of the body of the robot body (1); 
      the handle component comprises a limiting ring (3),  a handle (4),  a tensioning ring (5) and a spring (6),  the axis of the limiting ring (3) is parallel to the horizontal plane,  one side of the handle is connected with the connecting ring (2),  the handle (4) is positioned in the central hole of the limiting ring (3),  the handle (4) is U-shaped,  the tail ends of the two limiting rings are connected with one side of the inner wall of the limiting ring (3) close to the robot body (1),  the tensioning ring (5) and the spring (6) are both positioned at the inner side of the handle (4),  the axis of the spring (6) is parallel to the horizontal plane,  one end of the robot close to the robot body (1) is connected with a limit ring (3),  the other end is connected with a tensioning ring (5),  the axial line of the tension ring (5) is parallel to the axial line of the limit ring (3),  when the tensioning ring (5) is contacted with the middle part of the handle (4),  the spring (6) is in a stretching state; 
      the handle assembly has two and is symmetrical along the axis center of the connecting ring (2).

The utility model provides a cabin detection system. The cabin detection system comprises a multi-legged robot and a transparent plane frame,  the multi-legged robot comprises an equipment frame,  a camera and a plurality of moving supporting legs which act cooperatively. One side of the transparent plane frame is a plane,  and the transparent plane frame is used for being erected above an engine compartment in the mode that the plane faces upwards. The multi-legged robot can be movably placed on the plane of the transparent plane frame;  the movable supporting legs are arranged on the equipment frame;  the camera is arranged below the equipment frame,  a lens of the camera faces downwards,  and the camera is used for collecting images of the engine compartment through the transparent plane frame. The utility model provides a cabin detection system. According to the utility model,  the engine compartment image can be automatically acquired,  and after the engine compartment image is acquired,  whether key parts of the engine compartment are replaced or not and whether problems exist or not can be conveniently identified subsequently,  so that a judgment basis is provided for judging whether overlarge traffic accidents occur or not,  and a digital basis is provided for repair,  maintenance and price evaluation. 1. a nacelle inspection system,  comprising :  a multi-legged robot and a transparent planar frame;  the multi-legged robot comprises an equipment frame,  a camera and a plurality of moving support legs acting in coordination; 
      one side of the transparent plane frame is a plane,  and the transparent plane frame is erected above the engine compartment in a mode that the plane faces upwards;  the multi-legged robot can be movably placed on the plane of the transparent plane frame; 
      The movable supporting legs are arranged on the equipment frame and used for moving the multi-legged robot; 
      The camera is arranged below the equipment frame,  a lens of the camera faces downwards,  and the camera is used for collecting images of the engine compartment through the transparent plane frame.

The invention discloses a waist joint mechanism and a robot and relates to the technical field of humanoid robots. The waist joint mechanism comprises a waist ball seat,  a waist ball cap and a waist ball. A containing cavity is formed jointly by the waist ball seat and the waist ball cap. The inner sidewall of the containing cavity is provided with a first sunken part and a second sunken part which are symmetric. The waist ball is arranged in the containing cavity. The sidewall of the waist ball is provided with a first limiting protrusion and a second limiting protrusion which are symmetric. The first limiting protrusion is inlaid in the first sunken part. The second sunken part is inlaid in the second sunken part. Gaps are formed between the upper end face and the lower end face of the first limiting protrusion and the wall face of the first sunken part. Gaps are formed between the upper end face and the lower end face of the second limiting protrusion and the wall face of the second sunken part. The waist joint mechanism can have high impact resistance when the robot makes contact with the ground,  can enable the waist of the robot to bend down in multiple directions in the moving process of the robot. The waist joint mechanism has low requirements for manufacturing and installation precision and is convenient to produce,  simple in structure and light in weight. 1. A lumbar joint mechanism,  comprising : 
      the waist ball seat and the waist ball cover jointly form an accommodating cavity,  at least part of the accommodating cavity is in a spherical shape,  and the inner side wall of the accommodating cavity is provided with a first concave part and a second concave part which are symmetrical in the circumferential direction; 
      at least part sets up at least part in holding the chamber is spheroidal waist ball,  the lateral wall of waist ball has the first spacing arch of symmetry and the spacing arch of second in circumference,  first spacing protruding embedding first depressed part,  the embedding of second depressed part the second depressed part,  first spacing bellied up end first spacing bellied down the terminal surface with the clearance has between the wall of first depressed part,  the spacing bellied up end of second spacing bellied down the terminal surface of second with the clearance has between the wall of second depressed part.

The invention provides a humanoid robot waist joint and a humanoid robot. The waist joint comprises a first tile structure,  a second tile structure,  a first transition structure,  a second transition structure,  a first substrate and a second substrate. A first end of the first transition structure is slidingly connected with a first end of the first tile structure,  and a first end of the second transition structure is slidingly connected with a second end of the first tile structure to limit swinging of the first tile structure along a first arc line;  one side surface of the first substrate is slidingly connected with a first end of the second tile structure,  and one side surface of the second substrate is slidingly connected with a second end of the second tile structure to limit swinging of the second tile structure along a second arc line;  a second end of the first transition structure is fixedly connected with a third end of the second tile structure;  and a second end of the second transition structure is fixedly connected with a fourth end of the second tile structure. Through the scheme,  the robot achieves higher impact resistance,  and is lower on manufacturing and mounting precision requirements. 1. A humanoid robot waist joint,  characterized by,  includes : 
      a first tile structure comprising a first end and a second end extending along a first arc in a first direction; 
      a second tile structure comprising first and second ends extending along a second arc in a second direction perpendicular to the first direction,  and third and fourth oppositely disposed ends;  the plane where the first arc line is located is perpendicular to the plane where the second arc line is located; 
      a first transition structure including a first end extending in the first direction and a second end disposed opposite the first end; 
      a second transition structure including a first end extending in the first direction and a second end disposed opposite the first end; 
      a first substrate and a second substrate both extending in the second direction; 
      wherein the first end of the first transition structure is slidably coupled to the first end of the first shoe structure and the first end of the second transition structure is slidably coupled to the second end of the first shoe structure to define the first shoe structure to oscillate along the first arc;  a side of said first base plate slidably coupled to said first end of said second tile structure and a side of said second base plate slidably coupled to said second end of said second tile structure to define said second tile structure to oscillate along said second arc;  and the second end of the first transition structure is fixedly connected with the third end of the second tile structure,  and the second end of the second transition structure is fixedly connected with the fourth end of the second tile structure.

The invention relates to the field of self-service shopping,  in particular to an unmanned store remote monitoring management system and method,  and the system comprises a background monitoring management system,  a first monitoring module disposed at an unmanned store entrance,  a second monitoring module disposed at an unmanned store exit,  and a third monitoring module disposed at an unmanned storeshopping area. The remote monitoring and management system for the unmanned store further comprises a first voice module arranged at the entrance of the unmanned store,  a second voice module arrangedat the exit of the unmanned store and a video consultation module arranged in the shopping area of the unmanned store. The remote monitoring and management system for the unmanned store further comprises an access control module. According to the invention,  by arranging the first monitoring module,  the second monitoring module,  the third monitoring module,  the first voice module,  the second voicemodule and the video consultation module,  the monitoring and voice reminding can be conducted on the unmanned shops in real time,  th ebackground managers of the background monitoring management system can monitor the multiple unmanned shops at the same time,  and the safety index of the unmanned shops is enhanced. 1. The utility model provides an unmanned shop remote monitoring management system which characterized in that :  the system comprises a background monitoring management system,  a first monitoring module (41) arranged at an entrance (1) of the unmanned store,  a second monitoring module (42) arranged at an exit (2) of the unmanned store and a third monitoring module (43) arranged in a shopping area (3) of the unmanned store; 
      the unmanned shop remote monitoring management system further comprises a first voice module arranged at an entrance (1) of the unmanned shop,  a second voice module arranged at an exit (2) of the unmanned shop and a video consultation module (5) arranged in a shopping area (3) of the unmanned shop;  the first monitoring module (41),  the second monitoring module (42),  the third monitoring module (43),  the first voice module,  the second voice module and the video consultation module (5) are all in wireless connection with the background monitoring management system; 
      the unmanned shop remote monitoring management system further comprises an access control module;  and the background monitoring and management system controls the opening and closing of the entrance (1) and the exit (2) of the unmanned shop through the entrance guard module.

