The invention discloses a human-like self-conscious service management system based on artificial intelligence and block chain technology,  which comprises a water module representing a management layer,  a gold module representing a revenue layer,  a fire module representing a safety layer,  a wood module representing a research and development layer and a soil module representing a benefit layer,  which are connected through a central processor,  wherein the water module includes enterprise organization code units,  system orientation unit,  protocol unit and learning unit,  the enterprise organization code unit is digital information registered by the enterprise with the relevant department,  the development orientation unit is enterprise system information negotiated by management personnel,  theagreement unit is labor agreement or commercial agreement signed between the enterprise and employees or customers,  and the learning unit is the employee of the preset scoring organization who actively learns the learning information of the enterprise propaganda culture;  The digital information,  the enterprise system information,  the labor agreement or the commercial agreement,  and the learning information constitute the happiness value information. 1. Humanoid conscious service management system based on artificial intelligence and block chain technology,  its characterized in that :  the system comprises a water module representing a management layer,  a gold module representing a profit layer,  a fire module representing a safety layer,  a wood module representing a research and development layer and a soil module representing a benefit layer;  five modules of golden wood water fire soil all connect through central processing unit,  wherein : 
      a water module :  the enterprise organization code unit is digital information registered by an enterprise to a relevant department,  the system making and directing unit is enterprise system information negotiated by management layer personnel,  the protocol unit is a labor protocol or a business protocol signed by the enterprise and employees or clients,  and the learning unit is learning information for actively learning enterprise publicity culture of a preset evaluation organization;  the digital information,  enterprise system information,  labor agreement or business agreement and learning information form happiness value information,  and the happiness value information is sent to the wood module through the central processing unit; 
      wood module :  the system comprises a central processing unit,  a staff learning unit,  a fire module and a water receiving module,  wherein the central processing unit receives happiness value information of the water module,  the staff learning unit extracts and applies contents of learning information in the water module learning unit,  1 to 1 matched business protocols with completely creative values are provided for corresponding clients,  and the business protocols with the creative values are sent to the fire module through the central processing unit; 
      a fire module :  receiving a business agreement with an innovation value sent by a wood module through a central processing unit,  and comprising a security enterprise authentication unit and a legal unit,  wherein the security enterprise authentication unit carries out security authentication on a client enterprise in the business agreement with the innovation value to obtain an enterprise security value;  the legal unit carries out legal validation on contract contents in the business agreement with the innovation value to obtain a legal safety value;  the enterprise safety value and the legal safety value form safety value information,  and the safety value information is sent to the soil module through the central processing unit; 
      a soil module :  the system comprises a central processing unit,  a signing unit and a money arrival unit,  wherein the signing unit collects information for signing and sealing a business agreement with a new creation value,  the money arrival unit collects information for client enterprises in the business agreement to pay for the agreement corresponding party according to agreement,  the information for signing and sealing and the information for paying according to agreement form achievement value information,  and the achievement value information is sent to a gold module through the central processing unit; 
      gold module :  the system comprises a central processing unit,  a staff obtaining unit and a client obtaining unit,  wherein the central processing unit is used for receiving achievement value information of a soil module and comprises a staff obtaining unit and a client obtaining unit,  the staff obtaining unit is used for obtaining a corresponding labor agreement through an innovative business agreement after safety confirmation and obtaining a payroll reward,  and the client obtaining unit is used for obtaining a contract scheduled project through the business agreement;  and the payroll reward and the contract reservation items form value acquisition information.

The invention discloses a power system reliability evaluation algorithm comprehensively considering both disasters and human factors. The first step is as follows :  the transmission lines of the powersystem are divided into four types,  aiming at the transmission lines of different power systems and considering the influence of human operation and disaster on line reliability,  the reliability of the whole power system is calculated by synthesizing the reliability of all kinds of transmission lines,  including four kinds of transmission lines and other equipments of the power system,  the reliability including reliability evaluation indexes such as probability of power shortage time and expectation value of power shortage. The invention refines the influence of the external factors on the power system to the influence on the transmission line,  combines the influence of the disaster factors and the human factors,  perfects the reliability analysis of the power system,  and makes the calculation result more in line with the reality. 1. An integrated power system of the human factors and the reliability evaluation algorithm taking into account of a disaster,  characterized in : 
      1st step :  the power transmission line is divided into four kinds of the electrical power system,  the power transmission line are controlled only by influence of a disaster,  the power transmission line has an effect only by a human,  and the power transmission line is not affected by a disaster affecting both,  of the transmission line due to the impact being controlled by a human; 
      2nd step :  the power transmission line with respect to only be affected by a disaster,  the disaster taken into account the effect of the degree of reliability of the line is calculated reliability; 
      3rd step :  the power transmission line has an effect for only by the human,  by using the error to a human cognitive reliability analysis method calculates a degree of reliability obtained quantitative analysis operation; 
      4th step :  for a disaster affecting by both,  the power transmission line and by the influenced by a human,  through a transmission line of a disaster affecting reliability integration function will only be influenced by the reliability of the transmission line as well as only a combination of the degree of reliability by a person,  while taking into account the reliability of the calculated by the occurrence of a disaster and a human; 
      5th step :  a degree of reliability of a transmission line in a power system for each of the integrated whole,  the power transmission line and the power system comprises four types of other devices,  the reliability of the calculated overall power system,  comprising a reliability evaluation index is less than a desired value to the low power time and the probability of charge.

The invention discloses a method for preparing a through-hole-structure polymer porous material from snowman-shaped Janus composite particles. The method comprises the following steps :  1) preparing Janus snowman-shaped composite particles;  2) preparing n-octyl-modified Janus snowman-shaped composite particles;  3) preparing a high inner phase emulsion;  and 4) preparing a poly high inner phase emulsion,  removing the water phase in the high inner phase emulsion by using ethanol,  and carrying out vacuum drying at 60-70 DEG C for 12-14 hours,  thereby obtaining the through-hole-structure polymer porous material prepared from snowman-shaped Janus composite particles. The preparation method is simple,  has the advantage of accessible raw materials,  and can implement mass preparation. The prepared through-hole-structure snowman-shaped Janus composite particles have favorable permeability,  and can be used in the aspects of separation,  adsorption and the like. 1. Composite particles prepared using a polymer having a structure of the snow doll Janus through-hole method of a porous material,  characterized in,  comprises the following steps : 
      1) Preparing composite particles Janus snow humanoid
      1.1) Taking polystyrene hollow spheres dispersed in water to give a polystyrene solution,  adjusting the pH of the aqueous solution of polystyrene was 8-10,  at 60-70 °C under stirring to form a seed emulsion; 
      1.2) And the 3-(methacryloyloxy) propyl trimethoxy silane,  1.0 wt % aqueous solution of potassium per sulfate,  sodium dodecyl benzene sulfonate ultrasonic dispersion in water,  so as to form a monomer emulsion; 
      1.3) Drop wise into the monomer emulsion was then slowly in the seed emulsion,  to 70-80 °C for reaction;  the resulting precipitate was washed with water after the completion of the reaction is centrifuged,  washed with ethanol,  centrifuged,  and dried in vacuo 12-14 h after,  give a white powder that is Janus snow humanoid composite particles;

The invention discloses a human-robot contact pressure testing method. The human-robot contact pressure testing method comprises the following steps of S1,  inserting a recording rubbing paper betweena robot and a pressure sensor for measurement,  wherein the robot can leave pressing dent onto the recording rubbing paper and meanwhile the pressure sensor can help acquire the contact force F betweenthe robot and the pressure sensor;  S2,  extracting the recording rubbing paper between the robot and the pressure sensor,  scanning the recording rubbing paper through a computer to acquire a dent areaS corresponding to the dent on the recording rubbing paper;  S3,  computing the intensity of pressure P through the computer according to the formula of P=F/S,  and determining whether the pressure is safe. The human-robot contact pressure testing method applies Chinese traditional rubbing technology to modern robot safety testing,  and by acquiring the contact area via rubbing and computing the acquired contact area and the contact force,  can help calculate the intensity of pressure through the formula. 1. A method for testing contact pressure between a human and a robot is characterized by comprising the following steps : 
      s1 :  inserting rubbing recording paper between the robot and the pressure sensor for measurement,  leaving an impression on the rubbing recording paper by the robot,  and obtaining a contact force F between the robot and the pressure sensor through the pressure sensor; 
      s2 :  taking off rubbing recording paper between the robot and the pressure sensor,  and scanning the rubbing recording paper by using a computer to obtain an indentation area S corresponding to an indentation on the rubbing recording paper; 
      s3 :  and calculating the pressure P at the position by the computer according to the formula P = F/S,  and judging whether the pressure value is safe or not.

