The invention discloses a method for connecting injection-molded silica gel with a component. The method comprises the steps that the to-be-connected component is pre-arranged in a molding mould;  theliquid silica gel is injected into the molding mould,  and the liquid silica gel is immersed at the lower end of the component;  and the molded silica gel is demoulded after the liquid silica gel is cooled. A plurality of holes and/or protrusions are designed at the lower end of the to-be-connected component,  the holes are blind holes and/or through holes,  and the holes and the protrusions are inclined relative to the connecting surface of the component and the silica gel. According to the design of the method,  the contact area between the component and the molded silica gel is increased,  and meanwhile,  the lower end of the component and the molded silica gel are embedded into each other through the holes and/or the protrusions. By means of the method for connecting injection-molded silica gel with the component,  reliability of connecting of the silica gel and the component is improved,  and the method can be widely used in the field of moulds. 1. A connection element according to one of injection molding a silicone gum and method,  characterized in :  comprising the following steps, 
      S-1,  to which connections are arranged in advance in a forming mold element; 
      S-2,  in a molding die to inject liquid silica gel,  liquid silicone rubber of the immersion element lower end; 
      S-3,  silica gel after cooling the molded silica gel mold to be liquid.

The invention provides a hexapod robot obstacle avoidance method based on fuzzy Q learning. The method comprises the steps that a hexapod robot measures the obstacle distance around the robot througha front ultrasonic sensor and converts the measured obstacle distance into a finite state set through fuzzy inference;  according to the finite state set,  obstacle avoidance simulation modeling is carried out in a simulation platform;  a Q learning algorithm is used to learn the action taken by the hexapod robot in the corresponding state;  the state set of the hexapod robot in the current state is determined;  fuzzy inference is used to determine the action set of the hexapod robot;  and the actions are fused to determine the next action. The obstacle avoidance method can realize a great obstacleavoidance effect in an environment where the number of obstacles is large,  and has a good market prospect. 1. A six-legged robot obstacle avoidance method based on fuzzy Q learning is characterized by comprising the following steps : 
      step 1,  measuring the distance of obstacles around a hexapod robot through an ultrasonic sensor at the front part of the hexapod robot,  and converting the measured distance of the obstacles into a limited state set through fuzzy reasoning; 
      step 2,  carrying out obstacle avoidance simulation modeling in a simulation platform according to a limited state set,  and then learning the action to be taken by the hexapod robot in the corresponding state by utilizing a Q learning algorithm; 
      and 3,  determining a state set of the hexapod robot in the current state,  determining an action set of the hexapod robot by using fuzzy reasoning,  and fusing the actions to determine the next action.

