The invention discloses a 17 degree of freedom humanoid robot and a control method thereof. The robot comprises multiple groups of sensor arrays,  a tracking detection module and a control module,  wherein the multiple groups of sensor arrays are arranged on forefeet and heels of two feet of the robot;  each group of sensor arrays comprises at least four sensors;  when being located in specified paths,  the sensors generate sensing signals;  the tracking detection module is used for respectively judging the forefeet deviation level and the heels deviation level of the robot according to the acquired sensing signals of the sensor arrays;  the control module is used for selecting a preset tracking strategy according to the combination of the forefeet deviation level and the heels deviation level to control the robot to move. According to the 17 degree of freedom humanoid robot and the control method thereof,  the deviation degree of the intelligent robot can be more accurately measured through the multiple groups of sensors,  so that the robot can be accurately controlled. 1. One octadecylenes degrees of freedom of the humanoid robot,  characterized in,  which robot comprises : 
      Multiple sets of sensor arrays,  two feet of the robot increases the fore-foot and rear heel portion,  each set of sensor array comprises at least four sensor;  when a sensor located at a prescribed path,  creation of a sense signal; 
      A tracking detection module,  according to the acquisition of the sensor array of the sensing signal,  the forefoot and the heel respectively judged that the robot the degree of displacement offset levels; 
      The control module,  in accordance with the degree of displacement of the fore-foot and hind paw from tracking strategy to select a preset combination,  control the robot motion.

The invention discloses a method for controlling the balance of a quasi-humanoid robot. The method comprises the steps that according to bending angles of all the joints of a robot body and known robot part sizes,  the gravity center and lower limb joint positions of the robot are calculated;  according to the state of the robot,  the ideal angles,  for keeping the balance,  of ankle joints and/or hip joints are calculated;  the bending angles,  obtained by a sensor,  of the ankle joints and/or hip joints are replaced by using the ideal angles,  for keeping the balance,  of ankle joints and/or hip joints. Control is performed through the method,  the robot can dynamically maintain the balance in real time,  and the computation complexity is smaller. 1. A balance control method for a humanoid robot is characterized by comprising the following steps : 
      step 1,  calculating the gravity center and the position of a lower limb joint of the robot according to the bending angle of the whole body joint of the robot acquired by a sensor and the known size of a robot part; 
      step 2,  calculating an ideal angle for maintaining balance of the ankle joint and/or the hip joint according to the state of the robot; 
      and 3,  replacing the angle of the ankle joint and/or the hip joint bending acquired by the sensor in the step 1 with the ideal angle for maintaining balance of the ankle joint and/or the hip joint.

