A thumb proximal knuckle detecting and driving mechanism relates to a device used for detecting motion states of the thumb proximal knuckle of a human hand and feeding back a force born by the corresponding thumb proximal knuckle of a slave hand. In order to overcome the shortcomings that as a conventional force feedback device joint measurement mechanism is separated from a force feedback mechanism,  the system is complicated,  the structure is bulky,  the maintenance is difficult,  bidirectional active driving cannot be realized and the price is high,  a joint detection mechanism and the force feedback mechanism are integrated,  and a unique connection mode and a skillful joint measurement point layout are adopted. Therefore,  when an operator uses the equipment,  detected fingers can maintain the flexibility to the utmost extent,  the motion states can be accurately detected,  the finger joints of the controlled slave hand can perform coordinated consistent actions together with the corresponding finger joints of the operator,  and the force conditions of the slave hand in specific working environments can be fed back to the operator,  so that the immediacy sense of virtual reality or remote operation is enhanced. 1. A thumb proximal knuckle detecting the driving device,  for use with a computer,  the robot interaction device of the humanoid hands,  knuckles base (5),  by the base of the thumb proximal knuckle base (4) and drive components (111); 
