The present invention discloses a legged robot state sensing system based on a dual core processing technology,  wherein a dual core system structure is adopted,  and a SOPC technology is adopted to embed two RISC embedded processor NIOS II soft cores in a chip based on a FPGA core unit to achieve the structure. One soft core is used to establish a data acquisition kernel having a data acquisition function,  and the other soft core is used to establish a data processing kernel having a data processing and communication function. Data interaction of the two kernels is achieved through a mailbox kernel Mailbox and a shared RAM memory. With the NIOS II B soft core,  complete information acquisition can be achieved,  while the NIOS IIA soft core performs a data fusion treatment based on the data acquired by the NIOS II B soft core. According to the present invention,  a state sensing technology facing the complex legged robot is adopted,  and characteristics of information completeness detection,  high speed data parallel processing,  real-time data communication,  high reliability,  and the like are provided. 1. A legged robot based on a state of perceived system core processing techniques,  characterized in,  comprising a core module and the external module;  RISC core module comprises an embedded processor,  mailbox RAM core module and the sheet; 
      RISC embedded processor is a core embedded processor,  for data acquisition by the data processing and implement NIOS II B soft core and a soft core consisting of a communication function NIOS II A;  NIOS II B NIOS II A soft core and connected with the on soft kemels RAM;  NIOS II B kemels NIOS II A soft core and a mailbox kernel module connected with a soft,  mailbox NIOS II A soft core and sheet NIOS II B soft kemels by soft NIOS II A RAM kernel module access NIOS II B implemented communication between the core and soft core; 
      The external module includes a power unit sensor,  limb servo controller,  the navigation system in combination,  a display and a buzzer LCD;  power unit sensor,  limbs soft servo controller core in contact with the navigation system and the combinations are NIOS II B;  soft NIOS II A LCD display and a buzzer are the man-machine interactive module connected in the core; 
      Nuclei NIOS II A for communicating with the external coupling module software bus module CAN;  outlining module for planning the coordination module; 
      The core module is based on the core module FPGA; 
      A power unit sensor analog to digital conversion module connected with the soft core NIOS II B;  NIOS II B the servo controller with four limbs CAN bus communication module connected to the soft core;  NIOS II B in combination with the navigation system navigation module connected to the combination of soft core; 
      A power unit sensor includes a flow sensor,  a thermometer,  a hydraulic oil pressure gauge,  the engine revolution,  the engine oil meter,  the power supply voltage sensor;  soft core through the power unit sensor data collected NIOS II B includes limb oil flow rate,  engine temperature,  hydraulic oil temperature,  hydraulic oil pressure,  engine speed,  engine oil sump and supply voltage; 
      The servo controller NIOS II B soft core limb extremity legged robot acquired feature data,  feature data includes joint angle extremities,  the load force,  and the foot-dimensional force and torque servo valve current; 
      Soft core by combining the navigation module acquires NIOS II B combined navigation data,  comprising :  a pitch angle,  roll angle,  a heading angle,  and three-axis angular velocity and acceleration of the triaxial longitude,  latitude,  height and speed.

A control system for an elevator includes a capture input unit,  a face detecting unit,  and a processor unit. The face detecting unit determines whether images captured about a scene of each floor include human faces. The processing unit calculates a weight of each corresponding floor with respect to the number of human faces in the images of the corresponding floor,  and controls the elevator to a floor with a maximum weight. An elevator control system includes : 
An image input unit for obtaining real-time images of elevator entrances on each floor; 
A face detection unit for detecting whether the real-time images of each floor transmitted by the image input unit include human-shaped images; 
A processing unit,  when the real-time image of a floor contains human-shaped images,  the processing unit sets the number of people waiting on the floor as the number of human-shaped images contained in the real-time image;  and
A storage device,  the processing unit stores the number of people waiting on the corresponding floor in the storage device; 
Among them,  the processing unit also calculates the weight of the floor according to the number of people waiting on each floor,  and controls the elevator to run directly to the floor with the largest weight among the floors.

The utility model relates to a rush repair tool for a power grid and particularly relates to an insulator replacing tool. The utility model provides the insulator replacing tool. Through arrangement of a fixing rod,  a supporting rod can be conveniently arranged on a cross arm of a strain tower so that a fixing efficiency and a fixing strength of the supporting rod is increased. Through a lever block and a rope which are used for tensioning a cable,  the cable is convenient to be tensioned and labor intensity of an operator is reduced. Through arrangement of fixing wire and a positioning wire,  the supporting rod can be fixed firmer and a safety performance during a replacement of the insulator can be improved. Through arrangement a reinforcing rod,  a stability performance is further improved during usage of the supporting rod. 1. An insulator for changing the tool,  characterized in :  including a strut(1),  one end of the securing post(1) is provided with a fixed(2) support(1),  with vertical supporting(1) rod(2),  elbow(3) fixed on one end of the rod(1); 
      A take up the cable provided thereon for wire ropes(4),  elbow(3) bend(3),  for setting a fixed pulley that(5) is arranged on the cord(4) at the crank(3) pin(6) disposed through the fixed pulley(5),  cable(4),  for connecting a cable hook(7) provided at one end and the other end of the rope(4) connected to take up the cable for an arbor potherb(8),  disposed on the pole(1) arbor potherb; 
      Supporting(1) bars(1) during use for preventing further provided around the fixing yarn and(9) for preventing rotation of the rod(2) during use,  a positioning wire(10) supporting(1) slide bars(1),  for setting a fixed wire(9) setting section(11) for setting a positioning wire(10) rod(1) on positioning unit(12),  for setting the bit line(10) through the positioning section is provided with(12) positioning holes(13); 
      For increasing the fixing rod and the(2) rod(1) is provided between the stiffener(14),  connection strength between the support arm and the(1) fixed(2) reinforcing rods(14) welded to one end on the support(1),  and at another end reinforeing rod(14) above the rod(2).

An advertisement board includes an electronic billboard,  a camera,  and a counting system. The camera captures images in front of the electronic billboard. The counting system receives the images from the camera,  and check the images to determine whether there is a person in the image. When there is a person in the image,  the counting system obtains information of the person,  and compares the obtained information with information stored before. When the obtained information is different from the information stored before,  the counting system outputs a counting signal for counting. A reader counting system,  including : 
A humanoid detection unit for receiving an image captured by a camera and detecting it to determine whether there is a human body in the image; 
A humanoid feature grabbing unit for obtaining information of the viewer when the humanoid detecting unit detects that there is a human body in the image; 
A storage unit for storing the information of the viewer obtained by the humanoid feature grabbing unit within a preset time; 
A comparison unit for comparing the readers information with the readers information stored in the storage unit every time the humanoid feature capture unit obtains the readers information to determine the readers information obtained at this time Whether it is the same as the information of the viewer stored in the storage unit,  and send a count signal when the information of the viewer obtained at this time is different from any information of the viewer stored in the storage unit;  and
A counting unit counts according to the counting signal received from the comparison unit.

The invention discloses a hip portion of an automatic robot. The hip portion of the automatic robot is characterized by comprising a main frame,  two lower limb assemblies,  two side lifting transmission assemblies and two sets of buffering units. The main frame is a framework with an internal accommodating space and comprises a first displacement opening,  two first pivot racks,  two second displacement opening and two second pivot racket;  each lower limb assembly comprises a pivot joint piece,  a leg piece and a first driving motor;  each transmission assembly comprises a pivot rotation piece,  a guide rack and a second driving motor;  each buffering unit comprises a front buffering piece and a rear buffering piece. The hip portion of the automatic robot has the advantages of simulating the effect of human walking,  effectively avoiding overstepping of the legs of the robot due to control failure,  and meanwhile can limit the degree of freedom of forwarding and backward movements of the legs of the robot as well as protect the legs of the robot from overlarge impact and further avoid breakage. 1. An automated robotic hip,  characterized in : 
      The automatic robot hip region comprises a main frame (10),  two lower limb assembly (20),  two side lift drive assembly (30) and two sets of buffer units (40); 
      The main frame (10) having a containing space of an internal frame,  comprising two 1st bit shift mouth (11),  two 1st pivot brackets (12),  two 2nd bit shift mouth (13) and two 2nd pivot brackets (14); 
      A lower limb assembly (20) includes a pivot link (21),  a leg member (22) and a 1st drive motor (23); 
      A drive assembly (30) includes a pivot member di (31),  a guide frame (32) and a 2nd drive motor (33); 
      The buffer unit (40) has a front bumpers (41) and a rear cushion (42).

The invention discloses a modular robot capable of being self-assembled into a multi-foot wheel-leg robot. The modular robot comprises a left leg component,  a main frame,  and a right leg component. The left leg component and the right leg component are the same in structure and are symmetrically mounted on the left and right sides of the main frame (II),  and each of the left and right leg components has five degrees of freedom. The front of the main frame and the rear of the main frame are both provided with quick connectors used for quick connection with other modular robots to form the multi-foot wheel-leg robot. Multiple motion modes provide the modular robot with fine terrain adaptability and high terrain utilization rate,  and the splittability feature allows for better maintainability and better fault tolerance for the modular robot and provides high functional customizability. A single module still has the capability of completing certain tasks,  and accordingly the modular robot has good market prospect. 1. For the multiped round leg may self-assemble A robot module of the robot,  includes a left leg member (I),  the body frame (II) and the right leg members (III),  characterized in : 
      The left leg member (I) and the right leg members (III) structurally identical,  symmetrically attached to the main frame (II) right and left sides; 
      The left leg member (I) comprises a foot decelerates the motor (1),  1st steering gear (2),  2nd steering gear (3),  the lower leg rod members (4),  3rd steering gear (5),  upper leg bar members (6) and a double rudder organ festival (7);  lower leg rod members (4) through 3rd steering gear (5) and the upper leg bar members (6) is connected,  has one rotational degree of freedom;  foot decelerates the motor (1) 1st through steering engine (2),  2nd steering gear (3) and the lower leg rod members (4) conjointly,  has two rotational degrees of freedom;  foot decelerates the motor (1) with the output shaft of the wheel (1-1) are connected,  thereby forming a round leg of the robot; 
      The body frame (II) are mounted before and after the front quick connector (8) and a rear quick connector (9),  the robot performs fast connections with other modules,  forming a multi-foot round leg of the robot.

The invention relates to a humanoid manipulator,  belonging to a hand component of a performance robot. A forefinger,  a middle finger,  a ring finger and a little finger which are respectively provided with two sway pairs as well as a thumb provided with three sway pairs are respectively fixedly connected with a palm shell,  wherein the forefinger,  the middle finger,  the ring finger and the little finger are in the same structure,  and the sway pair of each joint comprises an electric motor. The humanoid manipulator provided by the invention has the advantages that the structure is novel,  simple and compact,  the volume is small,  the weight is light,  the joints are reliably connected and are convenient to dismount,  the fingers are reserved with spaces for mounting sensors,  and the transmissionrelation is simple and clear;  the motion ranges of the fingers are wide and flexible;  and the safety is high,  the reachability is strong,  the fingers are flexible when in coordinated movement,  and the application range is wide. 1. One of the humanoid robot hand,  characterized in :  has two swinging pair's index finger,  middle finger,  ring finger,  the small thumb,  the thumb and the palm respectively having three swing back side of the housing is fixedly connected,  wherein the index finger,  middle finger,  ring finger,  the small thumb structurally identical,  swinging movement of each joint pair comprises an electric motor; 
      The index finger structure is :  1st gear units 1st motor and the index finger fixedly connected with the index finger,  forefinger and index finger knuckle fixedly joined in the 1st gear units,  1st speed reducer output shaft of the index finger and the index finger digit fixed connection;  2nd gear units 2nd motor and forefinger fixedly connected with the index finger,  forefinger knuckle fixedly joined to the forefinger base 2nd gear units,  in the 2nd speed reducer output shaft of the index finger and forefinger knuckle fixed connection; 
      The thumb structure is :  1st gear units fixedly joined to the thumb thumb 1st motor,  with the thumb in the thumb knuckle fixedly joined 1st gear units,  an output shaft of thumb with the thumb finger fixedly joined 1st gear units;  2nd gear units fixedly joined to the thumb thumb 2nd motor,  speed reducer and the lower knuckle fixedly joined thumb 2nd,  2nd speed reducer output shaft of the thumb in the thumb knuckle fixedly joined;  3rd 3rd speed reducer is mounted on the thumb thumb,  thumb base knuckle fixedly joined with the thumb 3rd gear units,  3rd speed reducer output shaft of the thumb knuckle fixedly joined to the lower; 
      1st gear units index finger,  forefinger 2nd gear units,  gear units thumb 1st,  2nd 3rd gear units structurally identical thumb and the thumb gear units,  each of the speed reducer structure is :  an electric motor with a fixed plate is fixed,  in the both ends thereof to a three-axis fixing plate and the lower fixed plate is fixedly connected,  on the both ends thereof to the second shaft fixing plate,  the lower fixing plate is fixed,  on the both ends thereof to an axis of the fixed plate,  the fixed plate is fixedly attached,  with the upper fixed plate rotatably connected to the output shaft via a bearing,  an output shaft of a gear is fixedly connected to the electromotor,  second gear idly on a shaft of a three over,  three empty fitted over the shaft second upper wheel gear,  gear five empty fitted over the shaft an upper,  four empty sleeve on the output shaft having gear,  fixedly connected to the output shaft six toothed wheels,  toothed wheels meshing engagement with the second gear one,  two and three intermeshed toothed wheels having gear,  meshing engagement with the gear four three toothed wheels,  toothed wheels meshing engagement with gear four five,  six meshing engagement with gear five gear,  the motor is a servo motor.

A table tennis ball return placement training device based on a simulation vehicle aims to meet the need of table tennis ball return placement training. N batting units of the table tennis ball return placement training device are fixedly overspread on a table top of one side of a table tennis table in an arrayed manner,  travelling wheels are mounted at the bottom of a travelling vehicle,  a humanoid simulation plate is fixed onto the travelling vehicle,  a driving signal input end of a travelling wheel driving circuit is connected with a driving signal output end of a control module,  a driving signal input end of a travelling wheel driving mechanism is connected with a driving signal output end of the travelling wheel driving circuit,  and the travelling wheel driving mechanism is used for driving the travelling wheels to perform two-dimensional movement. The table tennis ball return placement training device is applicable to table tennis ball return placement training. 1. Table tennis ball hitting position of the vehicle based on the simulation training device,  characterized in that :  it comprises a table tennis table,  N of the striking mechanism (1),  simulated car and a control unit; 
      Each of the striking mechanism (1) includes elastic hit the floor,  touch switches (11) and the center indicator lamps (12),  the elastic strike layer that is impregnated with this striking mechanism (1),  touch switches (11) of the detection surfaces arranged at the underside of the hit the floor,  the center indicator lamps (12) fixed in a resilient striking layer; 
      N of the striking mechanism (1) a side-by-side array was loaded with and fixed to a table tennis table on a stage; 
      Simulated vehicle includes traveling wheels (61),  the traveling vehicle (62) and human type analog board (63),  the traveling vehicle (62) of the bottom is provided with traveling wheels (61),  wherein the human analog board (63) is fixed to the traveling vehicle (62) above; 
      The control unit includes a control module (10),  the traction circuit (64) and the traveling wheel drive mechanism (65); 
      The traction circuit (64) of the drive signal input to the control module (10) of the drive signal output terminal is connected;  the traction mechanism (65) of the drive signal input terminal and the traction circuit (64) of the drive signal output terminal is connected;  the traction mechanism (65) for the ground-engaging wheel (61) as a two-dimensional movement; 
      N of the striking mechanism (1) of the touch switches (11) of the switching value signal respectively to the control module output terminal (10) of the N th switching value signal input connected; 
      N of the striking mechanism (1) in the center of the indicator lamps (12) of the center lamp control signal input coupled to a control module (10) the center of the indicating lamp control signal input terminal connected; 
