The patent refers to the field of 'counting mechanisms'. The invention relates to an advertising board,  which comprises an electronic advertising board,  a camera and a counting system. The camera is used for shooting an image in front of the electronic advertising board. The counting system is used for receiving the image shot by the camera,  and detecting the shot image so as to judge whether human bodies appear in the image or not;  when the human bodies appear in the image,  the counting system is also used for acquiring the information of readers according to the detected human bodies,  comparing the obtained information of the readers with the stored information of the readers,  obtained in preset time,  and sending a counting signal so as to count when the information of the reader,  which is obtained at the time,  is different from the stored information of any readers. The advertising board is capable of recording the number of the readers in a period of time without repeatedly recording the same reader. The invention also provides the reader counting system and a reader counting method. 1. One of the viewer's point counting system,  comprising : 
      A humanoid detecting unit,  configured to receive an image captured from a camera,  to determine whether the image to be detected and to the presence of the human body occurs; 
      Acquiring the unit characteristics a humanoid,  the detection unit detects in the shape of a human to human body is present in the acquired image information of the viewer; 
      A storage unit,  for storing a shape of a human within a preset time according to the viewer by the information obtained by the fetch unit; 
      A comparing unit,  for acquiring the feature obtained in the shape of a human as soon as each unit of the information of a viewer's point information stored in the storage unit with the viewer's point of the information is compared within the viewer's point,  to determine whether or not the information obtained at the time of the audience of the viewer's point of the information stored in the storage unit within the same,  and when the information of the viewer's point of the thus obtained with the information stored in the storage unit is different from any of the viewer is transmitted both a count signal;  and
      A count unit,  according to the count signal received from the comparing means for counting.

The patent refers to the field of 'fluid heaters'. The invention discloses a water heater. The water heater comprises an inner container,  a water inlet,  a water outlet,  a heat source,  an input device,  a display device and a controller,  wherein the inner container is used for holding a certain amount of water capable of being heated;  the water inlet and the water outlet are communicated with the inner container so as to deliver water which flows in and out of the inner container;  the heat source is associated with the inner container so as to heat the water in the inner container;  the input device is at least used for setting the number of persons who want to bath;  the display device is at least used for displaying a mark which represents the number of the bath persons;  and the controller is connected with the input device and the display device and is used for receiving setting signals which characterize the number of the bath persons from the input device,  responding to the setting signals and controlling the display unit to display the mark which represents the number of the bath persons corresponding to the setting signals. In the mode,  users can set the amount of hot water corresponding to the number of the persons who want to bath,  so that the use convenience is improved,  and energy waste is avoided. 1. A water heater,  characterized in,  including : 
      Inner container,  for receiving a quantity that can be heated water; 
      Inlet and outlet ports,  and the inner container communicate to transfer into the inner container and out of the inner container of water; 
      A heat source,  to heat the water within the inner container associated with the inner container; 
      An input device,  at least for setting the number of people want to bath; 
      A display device,  shows representative of the number of marks at least for bathing; 
      The controller,  and an input device and display device is connected,  for
      Receives the setting signal from the input device an indication of the number of bath; 
      In response to the setting signal,  controls the display device to display indicia representative of the number of people is adapted to the setting signal of the bath.

A hub device with an upper cover capable of bouncing automatically after being opened is mainly characterized in that a projecting stopping point is formed on a sealing piece of a through hole of a fixing seat,  which is provided with a pair of tube reed frame. The stopping point and a sector piece can be contacted when closing to the range with 3-5 degrees,  wherein the sector piece is rotated relative to the fixing seat,  arranged on the rotating shaft of a bracket,  and used for limiting angle;  and when the upper cover is opened from the zero degree,  the sector piece,  namely,  the bouncing action of the stopping point,  is utilized,  thus achieving the function of automatic opening. 1 . The upper cover can be automatically lifted up one by opening hinge,  an upper cover and a body disposed to have a folding electronic product,  the upper cover and the body when closed by a latch structure locked;  characterized in that the hinge comprises : 
      A fixed seat,  fixed to the interior of the body,  which extend inwardly from the fixing seat side and a through hole ; 
      A bracket,  secured to the upper lid,  extending into the through-holes in the stent has so that the stent can drive the upper cover relative to the main body is rotated to open or close the shaft;  the shaft is provided with a limit rotation angle of the sectors ; 
      At least a pair of tubular spring frame,  oppositely disposed within in the through hole,  each tube having a sleeve to couple the rotating axle body portion of the spring frame;  and the cylindrical portion has a pair of covered by said cylindrical portion so that it elastically to the shaft cut groove,  and the cut groove is formed a positioning piece extending downwardly at the position ; 
      A closure piece,  of the lid is closed with the fixed seat through-hole,  and outwardly forming a raised when the upper cover relative to the body close to 3-5 degrees with the rotary shaft of the fan shaped sheet makes contact when the compressive force is generated so as to start and when the upper cover relative to the body to close to 0 degrees such that the upper lid is deformed so that when the upper cover relative to the main body is turned on by the deformation restoring force of the cover is automatically lifted up to make the upper stop point .

The invention discloses a humanoid robot foot posture real-time detection system and a method,  which belongs to the automation field. The system comprises :  a DSP controller,  a three-axis acceleration sensor and an angular rate gyroscope;  the DSP controller gains a piece of static foot surface inclining information through the three-axis acceleration sensor,  and gains an angle variety value through the angular rate speed gyroscope,  and obtains the real-time foot surface inclining information according to the static foot surface inclining information and the angle variety value. The invention also discloses a humanoid robot foot posture real-time detection method,  which comprises the steps of :  obtaining the static foot surface inclining information by calculating the collected three-axis acceleration information;  obtaining the angle variety value by calculating the collected angle speed information;  and obtaining the real-time foot surface inclining information by calculating the staticfoot surface inclining information and the angle variety value. The humanoid robot foot posture real-time detection system and method provided by the invention can real-time and continuously measure the foot surface inclining angle. 1 . One humanoid robot foot stance real-time detection system,  characterized in,  system comprising : 
      DSP controller,  three-axis acceleration sensor,  angular rate gyro ; 
      DSP controller operable to three-axis acceleration sensor of the write control signal,  and from the three-axis acceleration sensor in the three-axis acceleration information is read out,  and the acceleration information are each an arcsine operation of each axis,  a top having a static tilt angle ; 
      DSP controller for write control signal to the angular rate gyro,  and is read out from the angular velocity gyroscope angular rate information,  and the integration is executed separately for each axis of the angular rate information,  to obtain the angle variation value ; 
      At time t=0 and the DSP controller is used for each axis of the static angle change value by summing calculated inclination surface of the foot,  to obtain real time information about the inclination of the foot .

The invention discloses a motion planning method which prevents fore-and-after leaning of a humanoid robot and a device thereof,  belonging to the technical field of the motion planning of the humanoid robot. The method comprises :  compensation angles are arranged respectively for the rotor angles of an electric motors for the hip joint,  the ankle joint and the knee joint of a supporting leg;  the corresponding compensation angles are respectively added on the planning angles of the rotor angles of the electric motors for the hip joint,  the ankle joint and the knee joint of the supporting leg. The device comprises a compensation angle setting module and an add module,  wherein,  the compensation angle setting module is used for respectively setting the compensation angle for the rotor angles of the electric motors for the hip joint,  the ankle joint and the knee joint of the supporting leg;  the add module is used for respectively adding the corresponding compensation angles on the planning angles of the rotor angles of the electric motors for the hip joint,  the ankle joint and the knee joint of the supporting leg;  wherein,  the electric motors for the hip joint,  the ankle joint and the knee joint are the electric motors arranged along the left direction and the right direction of the humanoid robot in the axial direction. The invention can effectively reduce the fore-and-after leaning phenomenon when the humanoid robot is supported by a single leg,  and improving the landing stability. 1. One method to prevent movement of the humanoid robot inclines forward and backward planning method,  characterized in,  including the steps of : 
      The support legs of the hip joint of the motor,  the motor and a motor rotation angle of the knee joint of the ankle joint respectively provided a compensating angle; 
      Of the supporting legs of the hip joint motor,  the motor and a motor rotation angle of the knee joint of the ankle joint angle is respectively increased corresponding to the compensation planning angle; 
      Wherein,  the motor of the hip joint,  ankle joint of the knee joint of the motor and the motor both in axial direction along the left-right direction of the humanoid robot motor.

The invention discloses a method for controlling the time of foot landing which can lead a humanoid robot walk steadily and a system thereof,  belonging to the field of robots. The method comprises that :  the feet of the swing legs of a robot are detected to judge whether the feet land or not;  if the feet of the swing legs of the robot land before the time of the programming pace,  the ankle of the swing legs is elevated;  if the feet of the swing legs of the robot land after the time of the programming pace,  the ankle of the swing legs is lowered. The system comprises a detection device and an adjustment device;  wherein,  the adjustment device comprises an advanced adjustment module,  a lagging adjustment module and a supporting adjustment module. The invention has the effect that the robot canwalk steadily in the actual environment by amending the programming dynamic pace of the robot and controlling the pace in real time. 1. One of the foot landing time of the stable walking humanoid robot control method,  characterized in,  method comprising : 
      Detecting whether the landed foot of a leg swing robot; 
      If desired the foot of the leg than the foot swing robot planning time advance landing on the ground,  the contact force between the floor according to the size of the foot is raised in proportion to the swing leg ankle position; 
      If the ratio of the foot of the robot swing leg landing time lags behind the landed foot planning is desired,  then the swing leg is lowered the ankle joint.

The invention discloses a motion planning method for preventing leftward and rightward inclinations of a humanoid robot and a device using the same,  which belongs to the technical field of the motionplanning of the humanoid robot. The method comprises the following steps :  setting a compensation angle to a motor at a hip joint and a motor corner at an anklebone of a supporting leg respectively;  and adding the corresponding compensation angle to planned angles of the motor at the hip joint and the motor corner at the anklebone of the supporting leg respectively. The device comprises a compensation angle setting module which is used for setting one compensation angle to the motor at the hip joint and the motor corner at the anklebone of the supporting leg respectively,  and an adding module which is used for adding the corresponding compensation angle to the panned angles of the motor at the hip joint and the motor corner at the anklebone of the supporting leg respectively,  wherein the motor at the hip joint and the motor at the anklebone are the motors axially arranged along the forward and the backward directions of the humanoid robot. The motion panning method effectively reduces the phenomenon of the leftward and the rightward inclinations when the humanoid robot is supported by a single leg,  and improves the touchdown stability. 1. One method to prevent movement of the left and right tilting humanoid robot programming method,  characterized in,  including the steps of : 
      Their respective legs of the angle of the ankle joint of the hip joint motor and the motor is provided with one compensation angle; 
      Of the supporting legs of the hip joint angle of the rotation angle of the ankle joint motor and the motor are respectively increased by a corresponding compensation angle schedule; 
      Wherein,  of the motors is a shaft of the motor and the ankle joint of a hip joint to extend along the longitudinal direction of the motor to a humanoid robot.

The invention relates to a robot walking control method based on the determined study theory. The method comprises the processes such as the establishment of robot walking model,  the establishment ofreferenced gait model,  the study on the neural network,  the establishment of constant neural network,  the completion of walking task by utilizing the constant RBF neural network,  etc. The invention overcomes the disadvantages of learning ability in the current neural network study and the control method and realizes the accurate study of the unknown dynamic model of a robot closed-loop control system along the periodic gait track of the robot within a local area,  and can study the effective knowledge of the system dynamics during the stable dynamic control process and apply the knowledge to the subsequent same or similar tasks successfully. The method not only can realize the rapid walking on the basis of energy saving,  but also provides the powerful support for the development of the humanoid robots. 1. A method based on learning theories to determine a robot walking control method,  characterized in comprising the steps of : 
      (1) establishing a model of the robot walk :  to establish an angular acceleration and the angular position of the joints of the robot as a state variable of the walking robot joint angle model,  the model comprising a pharmacokinetic model is known,  unknown kinetic model and bounded disturbance; 
      (2) establishing the reference gait model :  establishing a reference gait model,  to generate the desired gait cycle tracks,  each track of the state variables and functions as a robot signal; 
      (3) of the neural network learning :  according to step (1) established of robot walking model and the step (2) establishing a reference model building adaptive controller gait,  and embeds the RBF neural network,  Lyapunov stability theory based on the RBF neural network adjusts the weights,  the desired gait cycle the robot gait trajectory trajectory tracking,  and RBF neural network approximates an unknown kinetic model of the robot system; 
      (4) establishing a constant neural networks :  according to the determined learning theory,  neural networks RBF neurons of the locus of the robot system moves along continuously energized condition is satisfied,  with weights converge to an optimum value,  taking the weights after a period of time within each of the weights of the convergent average values as learning training results,  and using the results established constant neural network; 
      (5) using a constant finish the running task neural network :  one of Steps (3) an adaptive controller,  and the step (4) constant instead of the steps of a neural network (3) in the RBF neural network of the adaptive controller,  trajectory versus the desired trajectory of the gait cycle to implement the robot gait tracking,  constant neural networks are used to eliminate the effects of unknown dynamics model,  the desired gait cycle of the gait of the robot increased accuracy in tracking the trajectory path.

The invention relates to a parallel,  joint-type and walk-help ectoskeleton artificial limb applicable to paralytic,  which pertains to a rehabilitation engineering technical field and comprises a hip joint,  a knee joint and an ankle joint which are connected in sequence to form the ectoskeleton artificial limb structure of human crura. The hip joint comprises a single-degree-of-freedom drive mechanism and a harmonic reducer with a larger drive ratio which can output high torque;  the knee joint adopts a four-bar mechanism,  worm wheel,  a worm and gear mechanism to realize transmission;  flection of the ectoskeleton artificial limb is kept by taking advantage of the self-locking property of the worm wheel and worm and simultaneously,  the worm wheel and worm can deliver larger torque;  the ankle joint adopts a 3-RPS parallel mechanism with three degrees of freedom,  which comprises an upper platform,  three active branched guide rods,  a lower platform and a thenar support part so as to realize dorsiflexion,  plantar flexion,  inversion and eversion. The artificial limb of the invention has compact structure,  large slew range for every joint and can meet the requirements of actual movements of human body. 1. One suitable for use in a prosthetic bone joint of a patient paralyzed type help walk out in parallel,  comprising :  a hip joint,  knee joint and ankle joint,  hip joint,  knee and ankle joints are connected in sequence,  lower extremity exoskeleton prosthetic structure of a human body,  characterized in : 
      An ankle joint,  comprising :  an upper platform,  the lower platform,  the foot support plate,  1st driving one guide rod,  2nd driving one guide rod,  3rd driving one guide rod,  the humanoid leg jackets,  wherein :  1st driving one guide rod,  2nd driving one guide rod,  at one end for 3rd driving one of the upper platform is movably connected with guide lever,  1st driving one guide rod,  2nd driving one guide rod,  the other end being connected to 3rd driving one of the guide is movably connected to the lower platform,  the foot support plate is formed from two sides of the flap and is fixedly connected to the lower platform,  outer sleeve and an upper platform is fixedly connected to a humanoid legs;  knee joint,  comprising :  1st servo motor,  a four-bar mechanism and driving mechanism,  four-bar linkage includes upper leg exoskeleton,  the exoskeleton shank,  a rear linking rod,  a worm gear,  the drive mechanism includes drive gears,  and worm driven gear,  upper leg exoskeleton includes two plates,  a servo motor is fixed to the upper leg exoskeleton 1st intermediate plate both inside and outside,  the drive and 1st output of the servomotor shaft and fixedly connected,  and with the driven gears,  driven gears mounted on the perpetual shaft end,  the worm on the leg between two plates of the exoskeleton,  the worm and the worm wheel is engaged,  the other end of the worm gear and lower leg exoskeleton is connected via a bearing,  the worm wheel rotational center of the thigh bone is connected with a support shaft and the outer,  rear link and thigh support shafts are attached to one end of the exoskeleton,  the exoskeleton and lower leg of the support shaft on the other end is connected; 
      The hip joint,  comprising :  a needle bearing,  harmonic speed reducer,  a support base,  a hip support shaft,  a timing belt transmission pair,  2nd servo motor,  a cover plate,  a motor seat,  wherein :  2nd fixed to motor mount on the servo motor,  a motor seat secured to the support base,  2nd moment by a synchronous belt drive servo motor output shaft is transmitted to the secondary hip support,  the hip support shaft through the flat key with the harmonic speed reducer is connected,  on the cover plate is fixed to the harmonic speed reducer,  a hip joint and the knee joint of the exoskeleton thigh support shaft connection,  an inner needle bearing mounted on a support shaft of a hip joint,  a needle bearing mounted on the supporting stand; 
