The invention relates to a humanoid robot foot,  which includes a rubber foot bottom layer,  a foot plate,  a six-dimensional force sensor,  an upper flange,  a lower flange,  an inclination sensor,  a tactile array pad,  a signal processing system and a foot surface. The signal processing system is installed in the front of the foot plate,  the inclination sensor is installed in the middle,  and the six-dimensional force sensor is installed at the heel. When the robot walks,  the six-dimensional force sensor on the humanoid robot's foot detects the ground reaction force when the robot's foot contacts the road surface during walking The inclination sensor detects the inclination angle of the foot plate The tactile array pad detects information such as the contact position and contact status of the foot and the road surface The signal processing system collects and processes these information in real time,  calculates the ZMP trajectory of the robot when walking,  judges the state of the feet,  speculates on the walking road surface of the robot,  and sends it to the control system of the robot to provide a basis for the gait planning of the robot and improve the gait stability and naturalness of the humanoid robot when walking. 1. An anthropomorphic robot foot,  the mutual mechanical connection of the bottom layer comprises a rubber foot (1),  footrest (2),  six-dimensional force sensor (3) and a signal processing system (8),  characterized in : 
      A rubber foot bottom layer (1) direct contact with the ground,  foot bottom layer rubber (1) turn provided with a pad on top of tactile array (7) and the foot plate (2),  tactile array pad (7) is disposed an insulation mat (12) and a tactile array (13),  a rubber foot bottom layer (1) the size of the,  shape and the tactile array pad (7),  foot board (2) of the bottom surface consistent; 
      Foot plate (2) of the bottom surface,  the upper surface is planar,  upper surface with a boss or lower stepped portion and with the foot plate (2) a bottom parallel,  foot plate (2) placed in tactile array pad (7) above,  i.e. tactile array pad (7) mounted on a rubber foot bottom layer (1) and the foot plate (2) between,  foot plate (2) is attached to the front of the signal processing system (8),  mid-mounted with an inclination angle sensor (6),  footrest (2) to mimic the shape of the human foot instep (9) mechanically connected; 
      Six-dimensional force sensor (3) mounted on the foot plate (2) of the heel,  six-dimension force sensor (3) installed above which an upper flange (4),  six-dimensional force sensor (3) and the upper flange (4) by bolts (10) is mechanically connected,  the upper flange (4) by bolts (11) connected mechanically to the ankle joint of a humanoid robot,  six-dimensional force sensor (3) arranged below the lower flange (5),  the lower flange (5) from the bridge plate (2) mechanical linkage; 
      The signal processing system (8) mounted on the foot plate (2) of the front portion,  a real-time acquisition and processing six-dimension force sensor (3),  the inclination angle sensor (6) and tactile array pad (7) transmitted from the information,  and transfers the information via a communication bus to the humanoid robot control system.

